<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4476]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>No screening </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4477]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Consider risk reducing BSO (rrBSO) on individualized consideration involving Pt &amp; Clinician.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4478]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>2.</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>High Risk</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong> group</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4479]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>No screening except those who decline rrBSO.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4480]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>BRCA – 1:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4481]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Offer rrBSO @ 35 years when child bear</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ing is completed </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4482]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Protective effect</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> on CA Breast (risk reduction is 30 – 75% in CA Breast).</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4483]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>BRCA – 2:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4484]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>r</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>rBSO after 35 years can be delayed up till 45 years but delay would lose the benefit of risk reduction in CA Breast.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4485]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>HNPCC &amp; Lynch:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4486]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Bowel = 40 – 60%.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4487]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Ovary = 10 – 20%.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4488]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Uterus = 40 – 60%.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4489]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>r</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>rBSO + TAH due to risk of Endometrial CA 40 – 60%.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4490]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4491]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4492]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Che</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>moprevention Aspirin from 16 years of age</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4493]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Colonoscopy </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>every 2 years after 25 – 30 years.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4494]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>H – </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>pylori testing</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> after HNPCC</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> positive</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4495]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Role of </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>PG</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>D.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4496]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Role of </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>PND.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4497]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Risk Reducing Surgery:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4498]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>rrBSO recommended:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4499]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>30 – 75% reduction in CA Breast.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4500]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>2% risk of </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>primary peritoneal cancer</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4501]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Salpingectomy – if ovaries need to be preserved.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4502]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Radical </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Fimbri</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ectomy</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> – if Pt refuses BSO.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4503]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Removal of fimbria </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>at</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> ovarian junction.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4504]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Concurrent TAH is recommended when:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4505]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Lynch syndrome</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4506]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Prophylactic</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ally, if</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> chemo</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> is required</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> for CA Breast (tamoxifen)</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4507]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>When </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ERT is given for </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>hormone replacement</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> purpose,</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>(progesterone increase</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> risk of CA Breast</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>)</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4508]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Mastectomy </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4509]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Progesterone is avoided in HRT as it     es risk of CA breast.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4510]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Chemoprevention:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4511]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Pt with heredit</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ar</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>y ovarian cancer syndrome w</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ho have not elected for rrBSO or are trying to conc</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>e</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>i</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ve.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4512]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4513]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Pre – Op Evaluation before rrBSO:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4514]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Occult Malignancy 4 – 8%.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4515]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Rule out occult</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> malignancy</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> by TVS and CA – 125.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4516]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Surgical Procedure:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4517]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>BSO by removing all ovarian and tu</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>bal tissue except intramyometrial</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> part.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4518]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ligate</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> ovarian A</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>rtery</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> 2</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>cm away from ovary @ pelvic bri</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>m.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4519]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Menopause and HRT:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4520]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Recommended.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4521]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>HRT up to 51 years.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4522]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Small   in CA Breast but low</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> overall</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> and no impact on mortality.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4523]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Factors to reduce CA Breast on HRT:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4524]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Concurrent TAH.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4525]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Mastectomy.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4526]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Limiting use of HRT.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4527]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>BRCA – 1 Carrier has CA Breast that is typically E and </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>P</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> receptor negative.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4528]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>BRCA – 2 carriers are usually positive.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4529]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Recovery:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4530]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>After BSO – 3M</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>0</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4531]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Mastectomy – 3m</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>0</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4532]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4533]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4534]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4535]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4536]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4537]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4538]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[4539]"> </p>', 0);

