INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-book-t-mm-05-014-0', 't-mm-05-014', 'document_html', '<div class="mm-release-marker" data-mm-release="f94027611ab71565c9dfd689046bb4a24db921b97ef1453416d5acfa140ed605" data-mm-topic="t-mm-05-014" hidden></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7214]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>15. </strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>PROBLEMATIC BLEEDING WITH HORMONAL CONTRACEPTION</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7215]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The management of women who present with problematic bleeding while using hormonal contraception is challenging.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7216]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Before starting hormonal contraception, women should be advised about the bleeding patterns expected both initially and in the longer term.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7217]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>A pregnancy test is indicated for sexually active women using hormonal contraception who have problematic bleeding</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7218]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Clinically important bleeding patterns in women aged 15-44 years </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><strong>Scheduled bleeding</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Menstruation or regular withdrawal bleeding with combined hormonal contraception (CHC)</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><strong>Other bleeding patterns </strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Frequent bleeding </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Infrequent bleeding </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Prolonged bleeding </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Spotting </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Breakthrough bleeding </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Amenorrhea </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>More than five bleeding episodes within a reference period</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Fewer than three bleeding episodes within a reference period</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Bleeding episode lasting 14 days or more</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Vaginal discharge containing blood, that may not require the use of sanitary protection</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Unscheduled bleeding in women using CHC</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>No bleeding or spotting days throughout the 90-day reference period</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><em><strong>Bleeding episode:</strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''> one or more consecutive days of bleeding, bounded by bleed-free days.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><em><strong>Reference period:</strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''> a 90-day period of time during use of a hormonal contraceptive method</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7219]"> </p>
