INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-book-t-mm-05-014-1', 't-mm-05-014', 'document_html', '<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7310]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Could try a different POP Women may experience different bleeding with patterns was the traditional POP and the DSG POP </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>No evidence to support the use of two POPS per day to improve bleeding </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Although regimens such as estrogen supplementation or tranexamic acid may help to reduce bleeding induced by progestogen-only contraceptives in the </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>short-term</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> evidence does not support routine use of such regimens particularly </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>daily for</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> long term effect.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>In general, continue with the same pill for at least 3 months’ as bleeding may settle in this time. </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Use COC with a dose of EE to provide the best cycle control Could consider increasing the EE dose up to a maximum of 35ug. </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Could try a different COC but NO evidence one better than any other in terms of cycle control No evidence changing progestogen dose or type improves cycle control but may help an individual basis.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> CVR it may offer better cycle control than COC.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>There are no data on managing bleeding associated with the patch Continue for at least 3 months as bleeding may settle in this time.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>A first-line COC (30-35 μg E</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>E with LNG </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>norethisterone). ca</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>n be </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>considered</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> for up to 3 months continuously or</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> in the usual cyclical regimen (unlicensed).</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>No evidence that reducing injection </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>interval</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> for DM</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>PA Implies bleeding. However, DM</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>PA may be </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>given after a 10-week Interval</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>T</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>o reduce the duration of bleeding </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>episodes in</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> DMPA </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>mefenamic acid</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>500 mg twice (or licensed use</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>up</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> to three times</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>)</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> daily or </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>tranexamic</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> acid four times daily for 5 days may </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>be </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>effective</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> in the short form </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>but </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>confers</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> no long-term</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> effect.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7311]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[7312]"> </p>
