<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8626]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Not routinely given.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8627]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Used when there is need for cerv</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ical dilatation or use of specul</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>um.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8628]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Types of local Ana</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>e</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>sthesia:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8629]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Short acting</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8630]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Example:</strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> mepiva</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>caine</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>,</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> lidocaine and prilocaince require atleast 2 minutes.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8631]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Long </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>acting agents:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8632]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Example:</strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> bupiv</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>acain require at least 5 minutes to allow for onset of effect.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8633]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Cervical preparation before OPH:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8634]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Not used routinely</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8635]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Vaginal prostalglandis – 12 hours before procedure</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8636]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Cervical di</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>lators upto 6mm if needed.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8637]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Types of hysterscope:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8638]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>3.5mm or less in diameter should be used for diagnostic purpose.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8639]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Use the expandable outer working channels because they are associated with less pain.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8640]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Choice of hysteroscope depends on operator.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8641]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8642]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8643]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Distension media</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8644]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Saline</strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong> </strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>is recommended</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8645]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Reduced pain</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8646]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Better view</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8647]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Reduced vasovagal symptoms</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8648]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Less shoulder tip pain</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8649]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Effective in see and treat procedures.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8650]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Minimal risk with fluid overload</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8651]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Lesser electrosurgical complication.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8652]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Saline should be instilled at lowest possible pressure.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8653]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Warm saline appropriately according to body temperature.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8654]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Vaginoscopy:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8655]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Also called ‘no touch’ approach.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8656]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>It should be standard technique for OPH unless the use of vaginal spectrum is required.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8657]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Useful in following patients.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8658]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##4472C4; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Nulliparous</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8659]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##4472C4; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Sufferes of vaginismus</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8660]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##4472C4; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Virgo intacta</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8661]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##4472C4; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Genital track atrophy.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8662]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Prevention</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong> of infection following OPH:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8663]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Antibiotics not routinely recommended</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8664]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Must be given if suspicion of pyometra to prevet systematic infection</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8665]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Delay OPH if evidance of genital infection.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8666]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Documentation of OPH</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8667]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8668]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Related to findings:</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Impression &amp; description of vulva, vagina, cervix and endometrium</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Visualization of bot</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>h</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> ostia</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Details of congenital anomaly of uterus adhesions, cervical niches, fibroids, polyps and its FIGO types, RPOCS.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Uterocervical length when biopsy is taken or device</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> is fitted.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Related to technique:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8669]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Operator/ Surgeon</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8670]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Hysteroscopy/ operative device used</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8671]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Distention media</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8672]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Local anaesthesia (Agent, dose, route).</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8673]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Cervical instrumentation</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8674]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Biopsy performed.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8675]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Operative procedure performed</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8676]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Inhalational agents used</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8677]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Procedural success</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8678]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Complications</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8679]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Vasovagal reaction</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8680]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Uterine perforation</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8681]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Heavy bleeding.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8682]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8683]"> </p>', 0);

