INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-book-t-mm-06-015-0', 't-mm-06-015', 'document_html', '<div class="mm-release-marker" data-mm-release="f94027611ab71565c9dfd689046bb4a24db921b97ef1453416d5acfa140ed605" data-mm-topic="t-mm-06-015" hidden></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8841]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 16pt''><strong>15. </strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 16pt''><strong>STEPS OF POSTERIOR REPAIR:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8842]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Posterior repair steps:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8843]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The patient is placed in the dorsal lithotomy position. The pelvis and large intestine are prepared for surgery.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8844]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>A bimanual examination under general anesthesia is performed to differentiate between an enterocele and a rectocele.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8845]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> Observation of the perineal body is made to determine the extent of reconstruction needed</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8846]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8847]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8848]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The labia are retracted with interrupted sutures. The upper extent of the rectocele is identified. Allis clamps are applied to the posterior vaginal mucosa over this area. The clamps are elevated, creating a triangle.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8849]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8850]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8851]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8852]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8853]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8854]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Allis clamps are placed at the margins of the original hymen. An additional Allis clamp is placed in the midline at the top of the rectocele. A transverse incision is made at the posterior fourchette.</span><br><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>A Kelly clamp is inserted under the posterior vaginal mucosa, dissecting the posterior mucosa off the perirectal fascia. An additional incision is made in the perineal body, removing a triangular piece of skin, outlined by the dotted line. This will expose the insertion of the bulbocavernosus muscle. Only the skin of the perineal body should be removed, and care should be taken not to remove the underlying superficial transverse perineal muscles.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8855]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8856]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##404040; font-family: "Segoe UI", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The vertical incision in the posterior vaginal mucosa has been made, and the edges are held with Allis clamps. The perirectal fascia is dissected off the posterior vaginal mucosa. The apex of the rectocele is held in an Allis clamp. The dissection of perirectal fascia off the vaginal mucosa is started with a scalpel but is completed with the handle of the scalpel or with scissors.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8857]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8858]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>A finger is placed over the rectocele, pushing it into the rectum, thus revealing the margins of the levator ani muscles. Already, number 1synthetic absorbable suture is passed through the margin of the levator ani from the apex down to the posterior fourchette. Bydepressing the anterior </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>rectal wall downward with one finger and elevating the previously placed suture, the surgeon sees the margin of the levator ani more clearly, and placement of sutures becomes easier.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8859]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8860]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8861]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>After all levator ani sutures have been placed, they are progressively tied.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8862]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8863]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The excessive posterior vaginal mucosa has been trimmed away; the triangular defect in the perineal body can be seen. The insertion of the bulbocavernosus muscle is adjacent to the triangular defect in the perineal body.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8864]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8865]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The perirectal fascia is closed with interrupted 0 synthetic absorbable suture in the midline</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8866]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8867]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8868]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>A synthetic absorbable suture is placed at the apex of the vaginal mucosa and tied (a).</span><br><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The tail of the suture is left for a length of 20 cm.</span><br><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The suture (b) is placed superficial to the tail of the suture (a).</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8869]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8870]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The closure of the posterior vaginal wall is completed to the posterior fourchette. The former hymenal ring is reconstructed. The suture (b) is tied to the tail of the first suture (a) placed at the apex. The vaginal mucosa is approximated to the perirectal fascia to eliminate dead space</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8871]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8872]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The same suture completes the closure of the perineal body. Several interrupted O synthetic absorbable sutures are placed in the insertions of the bulbocavernosus muscles to reconstruct the perineal body.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8873]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8874]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8875]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8876]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8877]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8878]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8879]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The posterior vaginal mucosa suture (b) is placed in the subcutaneous tissue of the perineal body. Note that the suture marked a is still left long for eventual tying.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8880]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8881]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The same suture (b) that completed the closure of the posterior vaginal wall is used to close the</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8882]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>subcutaneous tissue and the insertions of the bulbocave</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>rn</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>osus muscles.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8883]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The suture marked a is the long end of the tie at the apex of the posterior vaginal mucosa incision</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8884]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8885]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8886]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The subcuticular suture (b) is placed in the skin of the perineal body from the apex of the wound immediately above the anus to the posterior fourchette. At the posterior fourchette it is tied to suture a.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8887]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8888]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The completed operation is shown, with the rectocele reduced and the perineal body reconstructed. Vaginal packs are not required. Bladder catheterization is rarely indicated.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8889]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8890]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8891]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8892]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8893]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8894]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8895]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8896]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8897]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8898]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8899]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8900]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8901]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8902]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8903]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8904]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8905]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8906]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8907]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8908]"> </p>', 0);

DELETE FROM content_blocks WHERE topic_id = 't-mm-06-016';
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-book-t-mm-06-016-0', 't-mm-06-016', 'document_html', '<div class="mm-release-marker" data-mm-release="f94027611ab71565c9dfd689046bb4a24db921b97ef1453416d5acfa140ed605" data-mm-topic="t-mm-06-016" hidden></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8909]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 16pt''><strong>16.</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 16pt''><strong>THE USE OF SURGICAL DRAINS:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8910]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Indications:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8911]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>1.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>To prevent fluid accumulatio</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>n</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> that can be the breeding ground for infection and dicomfort</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8912]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>2. </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>To charactorize fluid</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8913]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>3. To monitor leakage like ser</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ous/ frank blood, so that early detection of haemorrage can be done.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8914]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>4. </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>To promote tissue apposition</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8915]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>5. </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Where visceral repair has taken place to notice ana</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>s</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>t</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>o</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>motic leak earlier</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8916]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>6. </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Prophylactic drain with the aim </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>to reduce infection in clean woun</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>d is not indicated.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8917]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Complications of drains:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8918]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Infection</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8919]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Bleeding</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8920]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Hernia</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8921]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Kinking leeding to non fullfillment of purpose</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8922]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Material of drains:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8923]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Insert silastic material to reduce tissue reaction.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8924]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Types:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8925]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Collect fluid in bag or bottle</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Passive</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Active</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Open</strong></em></span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Closed</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8926]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>- </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Open drains</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> collect</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8927]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> material into guaze </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8928]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> pad or stoma bag.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8929]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>- Usually not common</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8930]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>in gynaecology.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8931]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8932]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Closed Passive drains:</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8933]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Examples Robinsons or nasogastric tube </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8934]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Work by differential pressure between body cavities and exterior</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8935]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Closed Active Drains:</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8936]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Also called suction drains</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8937]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Example radivac</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8938]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Valves prevent reflux of fluid back into wound </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8939]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Can lead to tissue collapse around a drain that can obstruct drain orifices</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8940]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Promote tissues apposition, leading to minimization of hematoma or seroma formation.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8941]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Suction force also keeps clear the drain from </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>debris</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8942]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Location of drains in Gynaecology:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8943]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>1. </strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Pelvis</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8944]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>2. </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Subcutaneous drains to prevent hematoma formation</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8945]"> </p>', 0);

DELETE FROM content_blocks WHERE topic_id = 't-mm-06-017';
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-book-t-mm-06-017-0', 't-mm-06-017', 'document_html', '<div class="mm-release-marker" data-mm-release="f94027611ab71565c9dfd689046bb4a24db921b97ef1453416d5acfa140ed605" data-mm-topic="t-mm-06-017" hidden></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8946]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 16pt''><strong>17. </strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 16pt''><strong>POST OP COMPLICATIONS:</strong></span></p>', 0);

DELETE FROM content_blocks WHERE topic_id = 't-mm-06-018';
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-book-t-mm-06-018-0', 't-mm-06-018', 'document_html', '<div class="mm-release-marker" data-mm-release="f94027611ab71565c9dfd689046bb4a24db921b97ef1453416d5acfa140ed605" data-mm-topic="t-mm-06-018" hidden></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8947]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''>17.1. </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''>HAEMORRHAGE</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8948]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Can be primary or secondary</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8949]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Primary haemorrhage</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8950]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Within 24 hours post op</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8951]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Causes</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8952]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Inadequate haemostasis intra op</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8953]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Slipped ligature</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8954]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Difficult to decide whether to reopen or not</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8955]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Delayed decision can lead to DIC</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8956]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Revealed haemorrhage</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8957]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Following vaginal surgery</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8958]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Packing can arrest venous bleeding </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8959]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Packing require anethesia</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8960]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Concealed haemorrhage </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8961]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Following abdominal or laproscopic surgery</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8962]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Collection can be inside the abdomen or within rectus muscles.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8963]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>S/S:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8964]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Abd pain</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8965]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Dyspnea</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8966]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Feeling light headedness</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8967]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Tachycardia</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8968]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Tachypnea</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8969]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Hypotention</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8970]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Cold clamy skin</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8971]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>GCS</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8972]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Management:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8973]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Packing – usually helpful in vaginal cervical procedure</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8974]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Exploration</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8975]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>In abdominal procedure</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8976]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Ligation of bleeding vessels</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8977]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Re – application of slipped ligature</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8978]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Intervention Radiology:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8979]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Helpful in cases when</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8980]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Bleeding is caused by aberant vessel which can’t be identified surgically or AV malformation</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8981]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Catheter is inserted into targeted artery</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8982]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Catheter is fed with radiological help, after insertion of cather, clotting agent is released for example coil, particles gel or foam to stop bleeding.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8983]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>It is not available @ all set ups. </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8984]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''><u><strong>DIC:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8985]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Following major Haemorrhage</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8986]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Major haemorrhage</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8987]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8988]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Release of procoagulants</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8989]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8990]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Stimulate coagulation activity</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8991]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8992]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Consumption of coagulation factors, clotting factors, platelets which leads to further bleeding.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8993]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Stimulation of fibrinolysis leading to release of FDPs</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8994]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8995]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Platelets</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>FDPs</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8996]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Clotting factors</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 10pt''>Fibrinsoluble </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>complexes</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8997]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Coagulation factors</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8998]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Interfere with cardiac functions especially    FDPs</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[8999]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9000]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Exagerate sock</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9001]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9002]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9003]"><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''>More bleeding</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9004]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9005]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Diagnosis</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9006]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Increased level:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9007]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>1. FDPs</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9008]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>2. Fibrin soluble complexes</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9009]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>3. Clotting time</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9010]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Decreased Level</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9011]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>1. Fibrinogen</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9012]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>2. Platelets</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9013]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Treatment:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9014]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>1. Treat the underlying cause, stop haemorrhage</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9015]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>2. Correct clotting disorder</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9016]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>FFP – most coagulaion factors</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> are present but </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> low in </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>fibrinogen.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9017]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Cryoprecipitate – more fibrinogen than FFP but more Ani Thromnin </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>III</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong> </strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9018]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The amount and type of given product should be determind on the type of coagulopathy and by the haematologist</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9019]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Coagulopathy resolves in 24 – 48 hours while thrombocytopenia resolves within a week.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9020]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Rotational thromboelastometry (TEG/ROTEM)  test is used by some units to assess coagulation and fibrinolysis, it guides regarding transfusion therapy in patients with significant haemorrhage however reference ranges vary between pregnant and non pregnant population.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9021]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Secondary haemorrhage:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9022]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Occurs after 7 – 14 days.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9023]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>More common in vaginal procedures</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9024]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Has an infective aetiology</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9025]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Can be because of retained products of conception</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9026]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Treatment is antibiotics along with culture and sensitivity of infective agent </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9027]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Correct the cause.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9028]"> </p>', 0);

