INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-book-t-mm-06-019-0', 't-mm-06-019', 'document_html', '<div class="mm-release-marker" data-mm-release="f94027611ab71565c9dfd689046bb4a24db921b97ef1453416d5acfa140ed605" data-mm-topic="t-mm-06-019" hidden></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9029]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''>17.2. </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''>HAEMATOMAS:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9030]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Hematoma is a bruise Collection of blood underneath the skin or with in a cavity.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9031]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Assessment of risks and benefits of stopping or continuing antiplatelets like aspirin, clexane, warfarin or NOAC.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9032]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Consult the concerned consultant if patient had heart problem for which she is taking anticoagulant.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9033]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Wound H</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>a</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>ematoma:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9034]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>1. Superficial hematoa underneath the skin </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9035]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>2. Can cause pain, super imposd infection and fever</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9036]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Treatment</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9037]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Treat underlying cause</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9038]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Most can be managed expectantly</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9039]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Surgery is necessary in case of enlarging hematoma causing pain, discomfort and complication.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9040]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Under anesthesia</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9041]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Incision + Drainage + ligation of bleeding vessels.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9042]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Consider antibiotics if necessary.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9043]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Vault H</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>a</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>ematoma:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9044]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Relatively common after hystrectomy 20%</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9045]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Majority treated by antibiotics alone.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9046]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Indication of surgery:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9047]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Sepsis</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9048]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Persistent symptoms like pain</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9049]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Large sized</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9050]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Procedure:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9051]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Approach vaginally (very less likely abdominal approach).</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9052]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Remove one or two sutures</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9053]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Introduce finger, avoid instruments</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9054]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Bimanual compression to expell hematoma</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9055]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Meticulus examination to look for bleeding point, Mostly no cause is found</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9056]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Place a large bore or corrugated drain and fix it with vaginal mucousa with purse string sutures.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9057]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Close the vault if it was sutured continuosly in primary surgery.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9058]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Pack is not essential but provide additional haemostatic support in case of significant ozing.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9059]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9060]"> </p>
<div class="mm-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0"><table class="mm-table" style="border-collapse:collapse;margin-left:0pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;"><colgroup><col style="width:126.05pt;"><col style="width:125.45pt;"></colgroup><tbody><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="353" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:132.25pt;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;">Procedure</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:132.2pt;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;">Hematoma</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:132.25pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Episiotomy</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:132.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Perineal haematoma</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:132.25pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Keilland’s forceps</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:132.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Broad ligament haematoma</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:132.25pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Vaginal hystrectomy</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:132.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Vault haematoma</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:132.25pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Elective C/S</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:132.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Wound haematoma</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:132.25pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Sacrospinous fixation</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:132.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Paravaginal haematoma</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9061]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9062]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Key points about h</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>a</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>ematomas:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9063]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Most of h</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>a</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ematomas are managed conservatively</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9064]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Risk of  stopping anticoagulation must be borne in mind as patients are @ risk of VTE</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9065]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Large hematomas can become infected </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9066]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Consider drains when hematomas are managed surgically</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9067]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Vault hematomas mostly does not indicte return to theatre</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9068]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Broad ligament hematomas must be considered when clinical findings are not in keeping with symptoms.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9069]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9070]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9071]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9072]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9073]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9074]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[9075]"> </p>
