<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[11965]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Uncontrolled B.P despite 3 classes</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> of antihypertensive</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> with appropriate doses.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[11966]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>O</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sub>2</sub></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> sat &lt; 90%</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[11967]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Progressive deterioration</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> in</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> LFT’S, RFT’S, hemolysis, low Plt.</span></p>
