td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:71.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Subfertility </p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:121.5pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">- Ovulation occurs</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">- 1.5% General population.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">- 2.3% among infertile.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">- AUB</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:103.5pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">0.5% of reproductive age.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">- 24% - mild.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">- Sexual maturity affected if hypo in childhood ovulation not occurs.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"> </p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:108pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">- 2 – 4%.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">- poor fertility outcome</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><figure class="mm-figure" data-mm-figure-id="b91480d8b625825d832f65f6" data-mm-topic-id="t-mm-08-043"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Source figure b91480d8b625825d832f65f6" viewbox="428625 -19050 628650 295275" preserveaspectratio="xMidYMid meet" data-mm-object-manifest="a85ff556c67c1dabfd692c69a02704daec5418d791aadd68c26dc4c0d231f6a3"><defs><marker id="arrow-end-2c62a8e1dd70ffd15c2d" markerwidth="10" markerheight="7" refx="9" refy="3.5" orient="auto" markerunits="strokeWidth"><path d="M 0 0 L 10 3.5 L 0 7 Z" fill="#000000"></path></marker><marker id="arrow-end-030215e73267c7efc896" markerwidth="10" markerheight="7" refx="9" refy="3.5" orient="auto" markerunits="strokeWidth"><path d="M 0 0 L 10 3.5 L 0 7 Z" fill="#000000"></path></marker></defs><g data-mm-object-id="2c62a8e1dd70ffd15c2d" transform="translate(553926 27305)"><g transform="translate(0 0)"><path d="M 0 0 L 5080 130175" fill="none" fill-opacity="0" stroke="#000000" stroke-opacity="1" stroke-width="12700" marker-end="url(#arrow-end-2c62a8e1dd70ffd15c2d)"></path></g></g><g data-mm-object-id="030215e73267c7efc896" transform="translate(952071 38100)"><g transform="translate(0 0)"><path d="M 0 0 L 1 135890" fill="none" fill-opacity="0" stroke="#000000" stroke-opacity="1" stroke-width="12700" marker-end="url(#arrow-end-030215e73267c7efc896)"></path></g></g></svg></figure><span hidden data-mm-figure-member="b91480d8b625825d832f65f6" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:tbl[94]/w:tr[2]/w:tc[4]/w:p[5]/w:r[2]/{http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006}AlternateContent[1]/{http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006}Choice[1]/w:drawing[1]"></span>-   Egg,  fertilization.</p><p style=