90" height="59474" preserveaspectratio="none"></image></g></g></svg></figure> is </p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">                                       PTU causing hepatic </p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">                                       Toxicity in Neonates</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:102.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Overt = 0.5%.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Subclinical 25%.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Neurodevelopment delay in children if in 1st <figure class="mm-figure" data-mm-figure-id="1b28acae05b8209146ce2359" data-mm-topic-id="t-mm-08-043"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Source figure 1b28acae05b8209146ce2359" viewbox="0 0 123825 104775" preserveaspectratio="xMidYMid meet" data-mm-object-manifest="df9514855dc08d7303bbb1f67cf1aa38325fa22a9854be2558637e085b83b5e6"><defs><clippath id="clip-e8c05f6e8fecbed83ebc" clippathunits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M 0 0 L 154048 0 L 154048 125522 L 0 125522 Z"></path></clippath></defs><g data-mm-object-id="e8c05f6e8fecbed83ebc" transform="translate(0 0)"><g transform="translate(0 0)" clip-path="url(#clip-e8c05f6e8fecbed83ebc)"><image href="/uploads/content-images/maternal-mind-book/f94027611ab71565c9dfd689046bb4a24db921b97ef1453416d5acfa140ed605/media/866549440181cb5999a3a2f1bc4156e1e0db1172ad3b89b5e1e2b13d8f0bd057.png" x="0" y="0" width="154048" height="125522" preserveaspectratio="none"></image></g></g></svg></figure>.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">- transfer of anti-Thyroid Ab =&gt; Hypothyroid in fetus. </p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Treatment:</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">- thyroxine replant reduces adverse outcome.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><figure class="mm-figure" data-mm-figure-id="29aeac51e6b1cc522f24f145" data-mm-topic-id="t-mm-08-043"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Source figure 29aeac51e6b1cc522f24f145" viewbox="857250 19050 247650 295275" preserveaspectratio="xMidYMid meet" data-mm-object-manifest="ce3361078ed826f090db7ea11d2dffe4c534fa5926f48995f89338997e6ae864"><defs><marker id="arrow-end-2da96d027993e21760a5" markerwidth="10" markerheight="7" refx="9" refy="3.5" orient="auto" markerunits="strokeWidth"><path d="M 0 0 L 10 3.5 L 0 7 Z" fill="#000000"></path></marker></defs><g data-mm-object-id="2da96d027993e21760a5" transform="translate(981710 111010)"><g transform="translate(0 0) translate(1732 69272.5) rotate(0) scale(1 -1) translate(-1732 -69272.5)"><path d="M 0 0 L 3464 138545" fill="none" fill-opacity="0" stroke="#000000" stroke-opacity="1" stroke-width="12700" marker-end="url(#arrow-end-2da96d027993e21760a5)"></path></g></g></svg></figure>- Already taking treatment   dose 25mg.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">- Tests 4 – 6 weeks.</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:104.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">2.5%</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Treatment:</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Reduces adverse outcome.</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:135.05pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><figure class="mm-figure" data-mm-figure-id="2b7bf2bb84f7fb94807da119" data-mm-topic-id="t-mm-08-043"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Source figure 2b7bf2bb84f7fb94807da119" viewbox="1057275 -76200 238125 304800" preserveaspectratio="xMidYMid meet" data-mm-object-manifest="c5d6636bef0113871dac193db26bf8cfe994774f36106d6e638fadecc9b2cc6e"><defs><marker id="arrow-end-fe89d3b276d588e93b60" markerwidth="10" markerheight="7" refx="9" refy="3.5" orient="auto" markerunits="strokeWidth"><path d="M 0 0 L 10 3.5 L 0 7 Z" fill="#000000"></path></marker></defs><g data-mm-object-id="fe89d3b276d588e93b60" transform="translate(1185617 7620)"><g transform="translate(0 0) translate(0 76200) rotate(0) scale(1 -1) translate(0 -76200)"><path d="M 0 0 L 1 152400" fill="none" fill-opacity="0" stroke="#000000" stroke-opacity="1" stroke-width="12700" marker-end="url(#arrow-end-fe89d3b276d588e93b60)"></path></g></g></svg></figure>- 2 – 4-fold    ed risk of PTB.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">- TFT’S every 4 weeks once between 26 – 32 weeks.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Treatment:</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Not recommended.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15116]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 9pt''><em>Table </em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 9pt''><em>35</em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 9pt''><em>. </em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 9pt''><em>THYROID DISORDERS IN PREGNANCY AND POSTPARTUM</em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15117]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15118]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>THYROID DISORDERS IN PREGNANCY:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15119]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Demand of thyroid hormone    es by 50%</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15120]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Estrogen levels     es in pregnancy up to 18 – 20 weeks.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15121]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15122]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Thyroid binding globulin</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15123]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15124]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sub>Level of free T</sub></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sub>3</sub></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sub> T</sub></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sub>4</sub></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15125]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15126]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Production of T</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sub>4</sub></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> and T</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sub>3</sub></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> by thyroid gland </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15127]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>HSG levels    es in pregnancy in 1</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>st</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> trimester</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15128]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15129]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Binds to TSH receptors</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15130]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15131]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sub>Production of T</sub></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sub>3</sub></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sub> and T</sub></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sub>4</sub></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15132]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>From mid – trimester HCG</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15133]"> </p>', 0);
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-book-t-mm-08-043-1', 't-mm-08-043', 'document_html', '<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15134]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>fT</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sub>4</sub></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> and fT</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sub>3</sub></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15135]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15136]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>TSH levels</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15137]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Iodine requirements during pregnancy      es due to </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15138]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Consumption by thyroid hormone synthesis</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15139]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Iodine renal clearance</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15140]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Placental storage of iodine</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15141]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Uptake by fetus from 10 – 12 weeks leading to synthesis of thyroid hormone from 18 – 22 weeks.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15142]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Breast milk production</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15143]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Maternal thyroid hormone is essential for</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15144]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Maintenance of pregnancy</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15145]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Placental development</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15146]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Fetal development</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15147]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Fetus is totally dependent on maternal T</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sub>4</sub></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> prior to production of its owns thyroid hormone but remains dependent on maternal supply of iodine and T</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sub>4</sub></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> until birth.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15148]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Consequences of Iodine deficiency:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15149]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Baby</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15150]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Leading cause of neurodevelopmental defects</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15151]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Intellectual impairment </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15152]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Motor rigidity in children </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15153]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>In</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>f</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ant mortality</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15154]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>SGA</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15155]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Pre – term birth. </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15156]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Mother</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15157]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Miscarriage</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15158]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Subfertility</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15159]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Endemic goiter + hypothyroidism 30%</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15160]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Trophoblastic disorders</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15161]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Iodine Supplementation:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15162]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>No need of individual assessment</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15163]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>All pregnant and breast feed women </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15164]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>should take daily dose of 200 – 250mg iodine.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15165]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15166]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>From Iodine rich foods</strong></em></span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>supplements</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15167]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Milk</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>        </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>- 150mg in the form</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> of</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15168]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Yogurt</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>potassium Iodide.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15169]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Eggs</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>- Maximum 500mgs</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15170]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Fish (Marine)</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>don’t exceed from </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15171]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>from 500mg due to risk of toxicity.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15172]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Not more than</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15173]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>2 – 3 servings </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15174]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>per week due to </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15175]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>mercury contamination</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15176]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>&gt;&gt;</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>supplementation of</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> iodine 3m</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>0</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> before</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15177]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>pregnancy or as soon as pregnancy is confirmed</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15178]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Women with thyroid disorders can take these supplements</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15179]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Assessment of population Iodine status by </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15180]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>median urinary contraction of iodine</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15181]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>It is a maker of population</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15182]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Not used for individual assessment</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15183]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Diagnosis of Thyroid diseases in pregnancy:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15184]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>universal screening is not recommended </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15185]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>screening of thyroid disease is done on population that is @ risk of complications</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15186]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>type I Diabetes =&gt; 16% risk of OH</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15187]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>SLE =&gt; 11% risk of OH</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15188]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>SLE + </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Euthyroid</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> =&gt; 18% risk of pre – term birth</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15189]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>SLE + Thyroid dysfunction =&gt; 65% risk of pre – term birth</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15190]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>SLE with positive anti Ro anti LA = more risk of cardiac problems in thyroid dysfunction.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15191]"> </p>
