<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15767]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''>1.2.</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''>CHICKEN POX IN PREGNANCY:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15768]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>3/1000.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15769]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Incubation period: </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15770]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>1 – 3 weeks.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15771]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Infecti</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ous</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>: </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15772]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>48 hours before Rash till vesicles crust over (within 5 days).</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15773]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><u><strong>Varicella Zoster Contact: </strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15774]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><u><strong>1. Signify contact</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15775]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><u><strong>Symptoms develops despite VZ IG or antiviral PEP</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Pt presents with chicken pox.</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>24 – 48 hours.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Contact with GP</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Or midwife telephonic.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Avoid contact with </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>suspectable</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''> individuals.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><u><strong>Symptomatic treatment.</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>OFFER:</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Before 24 hours of rash</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Before 20 weeks.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Consider:</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>After 24 hours.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>After 20 weeks =&gt; symptomatic treatment only.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>      </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Avoid delivery for 7 days to reduce Neonatal risk.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>50% infection.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>23% clinical dis</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>ease</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Transfer </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>anti</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>bodies to fetus.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>less risk of </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>haemorrhage</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>, neonatal VZS.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Delivery within 7 days extremely hazardous.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Risk of transfer of virus with spinal needle.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Epidural is safe (as dura is not penetrated).</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Choose site with spared lesions.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>GA –    es respiratory morbidity.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><strong>Infection before 28 weeks</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Inform risk of FVS – 1%.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Refer to FMU @ (16 – 20 weeks</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''> or </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''> after 5 weeks of infection).</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>USG</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Amino – PCR DNA</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>MRI if USG abnormal.</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[15776]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><u><strong>No past history.</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Uncertain status.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Tropical/ sub – tropical</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><u><strong>Check Immune status.</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>IG – G status – (within 24 – 48 hours). </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>From booking blood – (within 40 </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>min</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>).</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Ig – G +ve</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>ig – ve.</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><strong>   </strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><strong> PEP</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>1. Oral antiviral as 1</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><sup>st</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''> line PEP</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Acyclovir, valaciclovir can be given from day 7-14</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>2.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>VZIG Given &lt;10 days:</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Of exposure.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Before rash in index case (if exposure is continuous).</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>If oral not tolerable or renal problem.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><u><strong>Explain The woman </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>that they are infectious.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>D-8 – 28 – if VZ immunoglobulins are given.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>D-8 – 21 – if not given.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><u><strong>5.</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><u> </u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><u>Re – exposure:</u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>1.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''> Check VZ</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>igG again if negative then give  Oral PEP or immunoglobulin</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>2.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''> Re – dosing of VZ IG after 3 weeks.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><u><strong>Postpartum vaccination:</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>2 doses 4 – 8 weeks apart.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Avoid pregnancy for 28 days (live Attenuated)</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Avoid contact with suspect</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>a</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>ble individuals.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><u><strong>2. past history of chicken pox.</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>99% predictive value</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Reassure, no Action.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''><u><strong>Significance of contact:</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>15 min in same room.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Face to face 5 min.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Contact in large ward.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Herperzoster.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>If on exposed axes.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>If in immune – compromised Pts (ed viral sheding).</span></p>
