prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>N. F</li></ul></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Agonizing pain requiring increasing analgesia.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Initially no obvious signs.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Later may have blisters and bruises.</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17204]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 9pt''><em>Table </em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 9pt''><em>37</em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 9pt''><em>. </em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 9pt''><em>Potential sites outside the Genital Track &amp; their Presentation:</em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17205]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17206]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Management:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17207]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>MDT:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17208]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Senior obs</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>tetrician</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17209]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Senior anesthetist</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>within 1 hour</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17210]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Senior Midwife</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17211]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17212]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Expert MDT: </strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17213]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>urgently if sepsis not responding to initial management.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17214]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Critical care Team:</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17215]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Urgent referral in severe or rapidly deteriorating cases of sepsis.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17216]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Indications for Transfer to </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>ICU</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17217]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>CVS:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17218]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Hypotension &lt; 90 m</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>m</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Hg systolic.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17219]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Lactate &gt; 4 m</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>m</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ol/lit persistent despite fluids resuscitation.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17220]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Suggesting need for vasopressor/ inotropic support.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17221]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Respiratory:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17222]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Pulmonary edema.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17223]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Need for mechanical ventilation.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17224]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Need for airway protection.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17225]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Renal:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17226]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Renal replacement Therapy.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17227]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Neurological:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17228]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Conscious level.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17229]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Miscellaneous:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17230]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>MOD</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17231]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Uncorrected acidosis.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17232]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Hypothermia.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17233]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Surviving sepsis campaign Hour – 1 </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Bundle</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong> of care:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17234]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Measure lactate. (Re measure if &gt; 2mmol/ lit within 1 hour).</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17235]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Obtain blood cultures.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17236]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Broad spectrum antibiotics.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17237]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>I/V fluids 30ml/kg crystalloids if lactate &gt; 4.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17238]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Apply vasopressors if hypotension after fluid resuscitation to maintain B.P MAP </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u>&gt;</u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> 65mnHg.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17239]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Antibiotics:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17240]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>I/V Antibiotics within 1 hour in women @ high risk of sepsis or septic shock.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17241]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Use of sepsis bundle improve compliance with urgent management.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17242]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Early fluid resuscitation of crystalloids with immediate bolus of 500ml in women with hypotension and lactate &gt; 4mmol, urine output be strictly monitored with urometer – 1 hourly.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17243]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Choice of A/B depends upon local epidemiology.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17244]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Where sensitivity not known = piperacillin/ </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>tazobactam</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> or Meropenem (for G – negative) plus clindamycin (for G – positive + Anaerobes) provide very broad cover.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17245]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Vancomycin is advisable in case of MRSA.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17246]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Switch to specific antibiotics in case availability of culture reports.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17247]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Add I/V Acyclovir 500mg TDS, as part of 2</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>nd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> line A/B in case of maternal deter</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ior</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ation with 1</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>st</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> line cover.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17248]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Pyrexia in labor &gt; 38</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>0</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>C or high =&gt; GBS prophylaxis.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17249]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Consider VTE propylene in sepsis.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17250]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Necrotizing Fasciitis:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17251]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Post birth wound can lead to serious abdominal or perineal N.F.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17252]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Infection causing necrosis of superficial and deep and </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>sub cutaneous</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> tissues.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17253]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>1.8/1000 C/section can lead to N.F.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17254]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Rapid for by GAS.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17255]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Spread </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>is</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> hematogenous or direct.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17256]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Visible signs are in later stages.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17257]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Require</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>increasing analgesic</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17258]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>increasing and</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> out of proportion pain due to edema and thrombosis of arterial supply to nerves leading </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>to increasing</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> demand of analgesia.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17259]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Obvious signs are later – bruises, Blisters.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17260]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Urgent involvement of plastic surgeon, intensivist, and infection specialist.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17261]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Treatment:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17262]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Piperacillin – </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>tazobactam</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17263]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>OR</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>          </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>+ clindamycin </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>+ </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Meropenem</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>                       </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>vanco</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>in case of </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17264]"><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>MRSA.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17265]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Clindamycin =&gt; switch off exotoxin.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17266]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>MRSA =&gt; vancomycin should be added.</span></p>', 2);
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-book-t-mm-09-015-3', 't-mm-09-015', 'document_html', '<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17267]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Streptococcal Toxic Shock Syndrome &lt; 50% </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>pt</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>s have classical sunburn rash.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17268]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Staph TSS =&gt; 100% sun burn rash.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17269]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17270]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Resistance to these A/B or allergies =&gt; consult infection specialist.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17271]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17272]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17273]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17274]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17275]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17276]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17277]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17278]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17279]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17280]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17281]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17282]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>(P – T – O)</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17283]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17284]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17285]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17286]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17287]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17288]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17289]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em>Table </em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em>38</em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em>. Important points regarding Antibiotics:</em></span></p>
<div class="mm-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0"><table class="mm-table" style="border-collapse:collapse;margin-left:0pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;"><colgroup><col style="width:179.8pt;"><col style="width:179.85pt;"><col style="width:179.85pt;"></colgroup><tbody><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.8pt;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;">Spectrum</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;">Points</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.8pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Co – amoxiclav </p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">No activity against MRSA or Pseudomonas Active against most streptococci, staphylococci (MSSA) anaerobes and many Gram negatives</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Concern about an increase in the risk of necrotizing enterocolitis in babies exposed to co-amoxiclav in utero</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.8pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Metronidazole </p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Only covers anaerobes</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Unnecessary if using clindamycin and piperacillin-tazobactam as each covers anaerobes well</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Used with e.g. cefotaxime as intrapartum prophylaxis for suspected chorioamnionitis if non-severe penicillin allergy </p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.8pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Clindamycin </p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">covers most GAS (&gt;89%) ; GBS (67%) so should no longer be used for GBS prophylaxis , Covers most staphylococci, including</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">many MRSA. and anaerobes Switches off exotoxin production</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Not renally excreted or nephrotoxic</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Associated with increased risk of Clostridium difficile superinfection</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.8pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Piperacillin – tazobactam.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Spectrum same as co-amoxiclav, but also many Gram positive and Gram-negative organisms, including pseudomonas</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">No activity against MRSA</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Renal sparing (in contrast to aminoglycosides)</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Poor activity against ESBL, producing coliforms</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Avoid in beta-lactam allergy Very poor CSF penetration</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.8pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Cephalosporins e.g. ceftriaxone.</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">No activity against ESBL producing coliforms, pseudomonas or MRSA</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Cover beta-haemolytic streptococci including GAS and GBS (but not enterococci)</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Should not be used if severe beta-lactam allergy Increased risk of C. difficle</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.8pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Carbapenems</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Very broad empirical cover, most Gram-negatives (including most ESBL-producers, anaerobes) Covers most Gram positives except MRSA CPE are resistant.</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Not for severe beta-lactam allergy With moderate beta-lactam allergy &lt;1% cross reaction </p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Excellent penetration including CSF</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.8pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Gentamicin </p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Mainly Gram negative cover (including most pseudomonas)</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">No streptococcal, or anerobic cover</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Inactivated in pus/anaerobic conditions Nephrotoxic and ototoxic, so usually limited where possible to a stat dose for sepsis. (For endocarditis a lower dose is given twice daily. and then serum levels must be monitored)</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.8pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Vancomycin</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Covers MRSA. Recommended option in severe penicillin allergy for GBS prophylaxis.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">No cover for Gram negatives.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Not absorbed orally, so always given intravenously unless treating C.difficile infection.</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:179.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Serum levels need to be monitored due to the potential for renal and ototoxicity.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Too rapid infusion can cause "red man syndrome" due to histamine release.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
