<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17556]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Fetal size crossing centiles &gt; 2 quartiles on growth centile.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17557]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Cerebroplacental ratio &lt; 5</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>th</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> centile or UA PI &gt; 95</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>th</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> centile</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17558]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Or </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17559]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Fetal size &lt; 3</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>rd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> centile</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17560]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Static growth:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17561]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>No forward Growth velocity in fetal size @ least 14 days apart.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17562]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>FGR in previous Pregnancy:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17563]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Birth weight &lt; 3</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>rd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> centile.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17564]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Early onset pre – eclampsia or FGR requiring birth before 34 weeks.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17565]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Birth weight &lt; 10 centile with abnormal Doppler studies.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17566]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>LBW:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17567]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Birth weight &lt;2500g.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17568]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>This term is no longer used term.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17569]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Symmetrical &amp; Asymmetrical FGR:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17570]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>This classification has no prognostic value but can be related to etiology.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17571]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Fetal size:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17572]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Measured by AC or EFW (combination of HC, FL, AC).</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17573]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Risk Factors:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17574]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Maternal Risks.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17575]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Medical conditions – strong association.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17576]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>DM with vascular disease.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17577]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Renal disease (moderate &amp; severe).</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17578]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>APLS.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17579]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Chronic HTN.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17580]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>SLE.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17581]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Cardiac conditions (congenital/ CHD).</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17582]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Stenotic lesions</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17583]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Valvular lesions</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>strong.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17584]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Complex cardiac CHD</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>association</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17585]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Asthma</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17586]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FF0000; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Anemia</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FF0000; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>   </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>less strong association.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17587]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>IBD</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17588]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Depression</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17589]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Age &gt; 40.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17590]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>BMI &lt; 18.5.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17591]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Gastric bypass (irrespective of BMI).</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17592]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Congenital uterine anomalies – septate/ </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>BI corporeal</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> uteri.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17593]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Antenatal Risks:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17594]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Alcohol:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17595]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Small amount – no association.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17596]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>1 drink – small association.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17597]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>4 drinks – double the risk.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17598]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Drug Misuse:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17599]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Cocaine </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>esp.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> crack cocaine.</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Has </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17600]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Marijuana</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 7pt''>association</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17601]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>So,</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> these should be stopped.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17602]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Smoking:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17603]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Dose dependent effect more in old women.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17604]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Stopping before 15 weeks – equals to background risk.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17605]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Nicotine replacement therapy vs e – cigarettes.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17606]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>e – cigarettes more effective than NRT.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17607]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>E – cigarettes less risk of FGR than NRT</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> P</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ts</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> with co &gt; 4PPm should be offered further testing for SGA/ FGR on moderate risk.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17608]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Caffeine consumption:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17609]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>300mg/ day in 3</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>rd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> association with FGR.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17610]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Recommended amount is 200mg/ day.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17611]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>IVF/ ICSI:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17612]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>No clear association.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17613]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Paternal factors no clear association, however changing paternity    es risk of pre-eclampsia and FGR</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17614]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Covid – 19:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17615]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Has association severe/ critical women should be offered USG Biometry &amp; further monitoring accordingly.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17616]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Bleeding in pregnancy except to due to previa has association with FGR/ SGA.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17617]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Gest hypertension or Pre – Eclampsia.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17618]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Aneuploidy Biochemical Markers:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17619]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Low PAPP – </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>A</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17620]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Or</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>    </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>should be offered Aspirin.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17621]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Raised </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>β</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> – HCG</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17622]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Low PAPP – A</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17623]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Raised </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>α</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> FP </span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 10pt''>Associations with </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 9pt''>FGR/SGA</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17624]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>(above 2 MOM)</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>So, Additional</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17625]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Raised inhibin</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>surveillance</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> is </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17626]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> (above 2 MOM)</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>recommended.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17627]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Low PPAP – A =&gt; Association with still birth.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17628]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>β</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> – HCG (above 4 MOM) no association with SGA.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17629]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>So, no additional surveillance should be done.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17630]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17631]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17632]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Prevention of FGR:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17633]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Reduce smoking – Recommended.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17634]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>All women who smoke should be assessed by co levels.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17635]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Ensure in house treatment from + </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>tobacco</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> dependence advisor.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17636]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Use opt out referral process.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17637]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Vitamin D 10mg throughout pregnancy Recommended uncertain role.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17638]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Folic Acid 400mg pre conception &amp; 1</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>st</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> recommended.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17639]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Prevent other pregnancy complications.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17640]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Balanced energy/ protein supplementation:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17641]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>birth weight.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17642]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Role is not clear.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17643]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Omega 3 long chain poly un saturated fatty acid – No effect.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17644]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Minerals, micronutrients &amp; vitamins – not clear.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17645]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Calcium supplementation </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>reduces</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> pre – Eclampsia but FGR association not clear.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17646]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Aspirin 150mg recommended</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17647]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Between 12 – 36 + 6 weeks to those women who are at risk of pre – eclampsia &amp; placental dysfunction.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17648]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>It reduces their chance of developing SGA / FGR.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17649]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>150mg OD @ night.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17650]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>LMWH – not recommended.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17651]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Surveillance tools for FGR:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17652]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u>Symphisio fundal height SFH</u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17653]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Routinely offered after 24 weeks.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17654]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>SFH &lt; 10</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>th</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> centile =&gt; Refer for USG.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17655]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Serial SFH more informative.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17656]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Plot serial SFH on growth charts.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17657]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>3 types of growth charts population base, standard &amp; customized.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17658]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Customized charts improve detection.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17659]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17660]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u>USG</u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> – core component of FGR surveillance.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17661]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Routine USG for AC/EFW don’t improve outcome.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17662]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Fetal size is measured by AC or EFW. AC is superior but inferior to combined measurement leading to EFW.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17663]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>EFW is measured by fetal parameters like FL, AC, HC.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17664]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Fetal size should be measured @ least 3 – weeks by headlock formula, in SGA every 2 weeks.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17665]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Plotting of EFW should be done on reference chart to determine centile.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17666]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Universal growth harts should be adjusted according to local data.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17667]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Amniotic fluid estimation either by, SDP (2 – 8cm), or AFI (5 – 25cm).</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17668]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17669]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u>Uterine Artery Doppler:</u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17670]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Predictive value of abnormal uterine artery Doppler is limited.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17671]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Can be used along mid trimester anomaly scan (18 – 24 + 6 weeks) to determine abnormal placentation &amp; therefore risk of early onset FGR also &amp; early onset pre – Eclampsia.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17672]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Also help in determining growth surveillance pathway.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17673]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Assessment of uterine Artery </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Pulsatility</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> index is recommended.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17674]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Assessment of uterine notching is not recommended as it is a qualitative assessment and it is common to have notching in 1</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>st</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup> </sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup> </sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>43% notching in 2</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>nd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> has similar sensitivity to PI.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17675]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Uterine artery Doppler in 3</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>rd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> helps in determining whether FGR is due to abnormal placentation &amp; it has moderate role in predicting adverse outcome for </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>SGA.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17676]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u>placental biomarkers.</u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17677]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Improve diagnostic of USG for SGA &amp; SB.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17678]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u>placental growth factor PIGF</u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>. &amp; </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u>soluble fms</u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> – like tyrosine kinase (s – flt) are recommended for diagnostic of pre – Eclampsia and placental dysfunction. But these are not recommended in non – hypertensive FGR diagnosis.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17679]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>More useful in 3</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>rd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> placental </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17680]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u>Placental morphology/ Biometry.</u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17681]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Under research.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17682]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u>Doppler Studies.</u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17683]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Umbilical Artery Doppler:</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17684]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>In all growth restricted pregnancies.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17685]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Reduces hospital admissions, neonatal mortality and pre – Term birth.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17686]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Abnormal can be defined as PI above 95</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>th</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> centile, absent diabolic flow reverse flow.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17687]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Ductus venous Doppler:</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17688]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Done if absent/ Reverse umbilical artery Doppler.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17689]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>In pre – Term FGR.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17690]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Can be defined as raised PIV above 95</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>th</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> centile (pre – critical) or reverse wave (critical).</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17691]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Cerebral Doppler:</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17692]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Abnormal MCA CPR/ UCR can inform monitoring strategies but don’t determine timing of birth before 37 weeks, but after 37</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>weeks it ca guide about timing of birth.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17693]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17694]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17695]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17696]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17697]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17698]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17699]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17700]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17701]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17702]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17703]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17704]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17705]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17706]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17707]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17708]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17709]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17710]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17711]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17712]"> </p>
