<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[17733]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''><em>Table </em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''><em>39</em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''><em>. Risk assessment for FGR and their referral Pathway:</em></span></p>
<div class="mm-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0"><table class="mm-table" style="border-collapse:collapse;margin-left:0pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;"><colgroup><col style="width:133.2pt;"><col style="width:68.65pt;"><col style="width:113.2pt;"><col style="width:95.8pt;"><col style="width:128.65pt;"></colgroup><tbody><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:133.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Risk assessment</p><ol style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">1.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>@ Booking.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">2.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>@ Mid trimester anomaly scan.</li></ol></td><td colspan="2" style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:177.9pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Screening for early onset FGR &amp; triage pathway.</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:97pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Screening/ surveillance pathway for FGR.</p></td><td rowspan="6" style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:130.9pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Reassess @ 28 weeks &amp; after any antenatal admission.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><figure class="mm-figure" data-mm-figure-id="c6146f31022d088c51a17fcd" data-mm-topic-id="t-mm-09-018"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Source figure c6146f31022d088c51a17fcd" viewbox="876300 47625 257175 457200" preserveaspectratio="xMidYMid meet" data-mm-object-manifest="9af9026098ad017281c5d25f285032496f434a408430b3687646d1659b7f91e0"><g data-mm-object-id="abd50465c936aaf4c1b4" transform="translate(910953 57331)"><g transform="translate(0 0)"><path d="M 0 318407 L 44903.5 318407 L 44903.5 0 L 134710.5 0 L 134710.5 318407 L 179614 318407 L 89807 408214 Z" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1" stroke="#5B9BD5" stroke-opacity="1" stroke-width="12700"></path></g></g></svg></figure></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Assess for serial complications developing in pregnancy.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">E.g.,</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">* Hypertensive disorders.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">* Significant bleeding.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><figure class="mm-figure" data-mm-figure-id="62f5f33bcfcb119c179f13b3" data-mm-topic-id="t-mm-09-018"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Source figure 62f5f33bcfcb119c179f13b3" viewbox="885825 19050 247650 495300" preserveaspectratio="xMidYMid meet" data-mm-object-manifest="e90a748abca25a2791b6f244c63c57d6777c2d6abfb7daeab32c5dd5a7ec02f5"><g data-mm-object-id="32c71758ac5eb32c914a" transform="translate(916487 29664)"><g transform="translate(0 0)"><path d="M 0 340179 L 47625 340179 L 47625 0 L 142875 0 L 142875 340179 L 190500 340179 L 95250 435429 Z" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1" stroke="#5B9BD5" stroke-opacity="1" stroke-width="12700"></path></g></g></svg></figure></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Serial USG from diagnosis till delivery.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:133.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Low Risk =&gt; no RF</p></td><td colspan="2" style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:177.9pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Anomaly scan &amp; EFW &gt; 10th centile.</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:97pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Serial SFH monitoring.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:133.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Moderate Risk:</p><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0F0" data-source-marker-font="Wingdings"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">⇨</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Obstetric History:</li></ul><ol style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 54pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">1.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Previous SGA.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">2.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Previous SB + appropriate for gestational age birth weight</li></ol><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0F0" data-source-marker-font="Wingdings"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">⇨</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Current Factor:</li></ul><ol style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 54pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">1.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Current smoker</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">2.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Drugs misuse.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">3.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Age &gt; 40 @ booking.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">4.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>BMI &lt; 18.5 &amp; other features.</li></ol><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;">e.g., eating disorder, bowel disorders causing weight loss.</p><ol style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 54pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">1.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Gastric bypass (even with normal BMI).</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">2.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Previous PTB/ 2nd  miscarriage (placental mediated). &lt;figure class="mm-figure" data-mm-figure-id="fb5c29a75d5a84cbb4637ff4" data-mm-topic-id="t-mm-09-018"&gt;&lt;svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Source figure fb5c29a75d5a84cbb4637ff4" viewBox="0 0 133350 95250" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" data-mm-object-manifest="07a6833a59bc5ec4a804e7ddd733b02d583fc24e8af72096d6bbfec25528a4dc"&gt;&lt;defs&gt;&lt;clipPath id="clip-16202a0e781e820977e8" clipPathUnits="userSpaceOnUse"&gt;&lt;path d="M 0 0 L 128905 0 L 128905 93980 L 0 93980 Z"/&gt;&lt;/clipPath&gt;&lt;/defs&gt;&lt;g data-mm-object-id="16202a0e781e820977e8" transform="translate(0 0)"&gt;&lt;g transform="translate(0 0)" clip-path="url(#clip-16202a0e781e820977e8)"&gt;&lt;image href="/uploads/content-images/maternal-mind-book/f94027611ab71565c9dfd689046bb4a24db921b97ef1453416d5acfa140ed605/media/94a331b39c0be30644ba464a8031f91c3253b7731d9451071132d5fa083a9a34.png" x="0" y="0" width="128905" height="93980" preserveAspectRatio="none"/&gt;&lt;/g&gt;&lt;/g&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</li></ol><p style="margin:0;padding-left:54pt;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p></td><td colspan="2" style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:177.9pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">* Anomaly Scan &amp; EFW &gt; 10th centile.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">* Require one off SFH @ 28/ 40 weeks.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">* Assess women with moderate risk for abnormal placentation and start aspirin.</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:97pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">* Serial USG from 32 weeks.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">* Every 4 weeks till delivery.</p></td></tr><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="9" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:133.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid currentColor;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">High Risk:</p><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0F0" data-source-marker-font="Wingdings"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">⇨</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Medical conditions:
CKD</li></ul><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;">HTN</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;">SLE</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;">APLS</p></td><td rowspan="2" style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:63.85pt;border-top:0.5pt solid currentColor;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"><figure class="mm-figure" data-mm-figure-id="14d685275e91e1d202a16e20" data-mm-topic-id="t-mm-09-018"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Source figure 14d685275e91e1d202a16e20" viewbox="1057275 809625 228600 228600" preserveaspectratio="xMidYMid meet" data-mm-object-manifest="33d2aa5a4b6f763d999362e5b85ee63f8e11da6ef1107c403faf22d6af33473b"><g data-mm-object-id="1eac7d7320c7f72dd7be" transform="translate(1069340 836344)"><g transform="translate(0 0)"><path d="M 0 20343.009225 L 105727.5 20343.009225 L 105727.5 0 L 179070 73342.5 L 105727.5 146685 L 105727.5 126341.990775 L 0 126341.990775 Z" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1" stroke="#5B9BD5" stroke-opacity="1" stroke-width="12700"></path></g></g></svg></figure>Consider aspirin 150 mg @ night &lt; 16 weeks as appropriate </p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">1. previous HTN</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">2. previous FGR &lt;3rd centile or ,10th centile born before 34 weeks</p></td><td rowspan="2" style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:114.05pt;border-top:0.5pt solid currentColor;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><ol style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">1.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Normal uterine artery Doppler &amp; EFW &gt; 10th centile.&lt;figure class="mm-figure" data-mm-figure-id="1b5ef25942f2d82eae714c6a" data-mm-topic-id="t-mm-09-018"&gt;&lt;svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Source figure 1b5ef25942f2d82eae714c6a" viewBox="1657350 38100 276225 133350" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" data-mm-object-manifest="6934ba5b4a932393eb3e2fa58a254649bbd4be829780b49bf4d36ee8b967b767"&gt;&lt;g data-mm-object-id="117435b5ad665a112d29" transform="translate(1669868 63500)"&gt;&lt;g transform="translate(0 0)"&gt;&lt;path d="M 0 13607 L 190501 13607 L 190501 0 L 217715 27214 L 190501 54428 L 190501 40821 L 0 40821 Z" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1" stroke="#5B9BD5" stroke-opacity="1" stroke-width="12700"/&gt;&lt;/g&gt;&lt;/g&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">2.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Uterine artery Doppler(N) uterine artery Doppler &amp; EFW &lt; 10th centile.&lt;figure class="mm-figure" data-mm-figure-id="2c6e083107c1f5de23d16a37" data-mm-topic-id="t-mm-09-018"&gt;&lt;svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Source figure 2c6e083107c1f5de23d16a37" viewBox="-1038225 28575 3162300 990600" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" data-mm-object-manifest="10b19795994cc9bd45dbe44dc1d8b6f9bb8e03d274e2be7d52bffdd57794d900"&gt;&lt;g data-mm-object-id="ef1ba8aec3d4a39ffc2c" transform="translate(-1023938 573270)"&gt;&lt;g transform="translate(0 0) translate(1556657 138793) rotate(270) scale(1 1) translate(-1556657 -138793)"&gt;&lt;path d="M 0 0 L 3113314 0 L 3113314 277586 L 0 277586 Z" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1" stroke="#5B9BD5" stroke-opacity="1" stroke-width="12700"/&gt;&lt;g data-mm-text-anchor="ctr" transform="translate(0 45720)"&gt;&lt;text data-mm-wrapped-line="0" x="1556657" y="152400" text-anchor="middle" xml:space="preserve"&gt;&lt;/text&gt;&lt;/g&gt;&lt;/g&gt;&lt;/g&gt;&lt;g data-mm-object-id="de400c35a04a8eea7753" transform="translate(1670050 54561)"&gt;&lt;g transform="translate(0 0)"&gt;&lt;path d="M 0 11271.25 L 183832.5 11271.25 L 183832.5 0 L 206375 22542.5 L 183832.5 45085 L 183832.5 33813.75 L 0 33813.75 Z" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1" stroke="#5B9BD5" stroke-opacity="1" stroke-width="12700"/&gt;&lt;/g&gt;&lt;/g&gt;&lt;g data-mm-object-id="8a2bfa09f656eb8f9cfb" transform="translate(1659255 913081)"&gt;&lt;g transform="translate(0 0)"&gt;&lt;path d="M 0 12223.75 L 198437.5 12223.75 L 198437.5 0 L 222885 24447.5 L 198437.5 48895 L 198437.5 36671.25 L 0 36671.25 Z" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1" stroke="#5B9BD5" stroke-opacity="1" stroke-width="12700"/&gt;&lt;/g&gt;&lt;/g&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;&lt;span hidden data-mm-figure-member="2c6e083107c1f5de23d16a37" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:tbl[104]/w:tr[4]/w:tc[3]/w:p[7]/w:r[2]/{http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006}AlternateContent[1]/{http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006}Choice[1]/w:drawing[1]"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span hidden data-mm-figure-member="2c6e083107c1f5de23d16a37" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:tbl[104]/w:tr[4]/w:tc[3]/w:p[7]/w:r[3]/{http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006}AlternateContent[1]/{http://schemas.openxmlformats.org/markup-compatibility/2006}Choice[1]/w:drawing[1]"&gt;&lt;/span&gt;</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">3.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Abnormal uterine artery Doppler &amp; EFW &gt; 10th centile.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">4.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Abnormal uterine artery Doppler &amp; EFW &lt; 10th centile.&lt;figure class="mm-figure" data-mm-figure-id="07171a545e8f1b36ccd1a64f" data-mm-topic-id="t-mm-09-018"&gt;&lt;svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Source figure 07171a545e8f1b36ccd1a64f" viewBox="1638300 133350 304800 114300" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet" data-mm-object-manifest="f7eae11f352d2776357594f60e1415730a7b856c10599c8d33228a9bb6f4ba83"&gt;&lt;g data-mm-object-id="3ce587f257f8ac7e24d0" transform="translate(1647825 161876)"&gt;&lt;g transform="translate(0 0)"&gt;&lt;path d="M 0 11429.75 L 216626.5 11429.75 L 216626.5 0 L 239486 22859.5 L 216626.5 45719 L 216626.5 34289.25 L 0 34289.25 Z" fill="#FFFFFF" fill-opacity="1" stroke="#5B9BD5" stroke-opacity="1" stroke-width="12700"/&gt;&lt;/g&gt;&lt;/g&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;&lt;/figure&gt;</li></ol></td><td rowspan="2" style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:97pt;border-top:0.5pt solid currentColor;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Serial user from 32 weeks every 2 – 4 weeks till delivery.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Serial USG from 26 – 28 weeks till delivery.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Serial USG from 28 weeks every 2 – 4 weeks till delivery.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Refer to FMU</p></td></tr><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="5631" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:133.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid currentColor;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;">Complex cardiac discase.</p><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0F0" data-source-marker-font="Wingdings"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">⇨</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Obstetric History:</li></ul><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;">Previous FGR.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;">HTN in previous pregnancy.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;">Previous SGA SB.</p><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0F0" data-source-marker-font="Wingdings"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">⇨</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Current Pregnancy:</li></ul><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;">PAPPA &lt; 5th centile.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;">Inhibin (2nd <figure class="mm-figure" data-mm-figure-id="97a6b91937f6167b383f50f3" data-mm-topic-id="t-mm-09-018"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Source figure 97a6b91937f6167b383f50f3" viewbox="0 0 133350 95250" preserveaspectratio="xMidYMid meet" data-mm-object-manifest="335a6c1aaeaeff78f98b10fec23a59459a158c02d81b3ee9907f7e84dcc690f2"><defs><clippath id="clip-e906fc438a13170e8f8d" clippathunits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M 0 0 L 128905 0 L 128905 93980 L 0 93980 Z"></path></clippath></defs><g data-mm-object-id="e906fc438a13170e8f8d" transform="translate(0 0)"><g transform="translate(0 0)" clip-path="url(#clip-e906fc438a13170e8f8d)"><image href="/uploads/content-images/maternal-mind-book/f94027611ab71565c9dfd689046bb4a24db921b97ef1453416d5acfa140ed605/media/94a331b39c0be30644ba464a8031f91c3253b7731d9451071132d5fa083a9a34.png" x="0" y="0" width="128905" height="93980" preserveaspectratio="none"></image></g></g></svg></figure>) &gt; 2 MOM.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;">Alpha FP (2nd <figure class="mm-figure" data-mm-figure-id="217c56f37cacf32700dc887c" data-mm-topic-id="t-mm-09-018"><svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-label="Source figure 217c56f37cacf32700dc887c" viewbox="0 0 133350 95250" preserveaspectratio="xMidYMid meet" data-mm-object-manifest="c45e67a62cd0359d34ecd9773b17b1670488d6cc193dab46a6b3f0f47967d63c"><defs><clippath id="clip-b2f4c01a680b8a962035" clippathunits="userSpaceOnUse"><path d="M 0 0 L 128905 0 L 128905 93980 L 0 93980 Z"></path></clippath></defs><g data-mm-object-id="b2f4c01a680b8a962035" transform="translate(0 0)"><g transform="translate(0 0)" clip-path="url(#clip-b2f4c01a680b8a962035)"><image href="/uploads/content-images/maternal-mind-book/f94027611ab71565c9dfd689046bb4a24db921b97ef1453416d5acfa140ed605/media/94a331b39c0be30644ba464a8031f91c3253b7731d9451071132d5fa083a9a34.png" x="0" y="0" width="128905" height="93980" preserveaspectratio="none"></image></g></g></svg></figure> ) &gt;2 MOM.</p><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Echogenic bowel.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Significant bleeding.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>EFW &lt; 10th centile.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Single umbilical artery.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:133.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Others:</p><ol style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">1.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Large Fibroids.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">2.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>BMI &gt; 35.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">3.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Congenital uterine Anomalies.</li></ol></td><td colspan="2" style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:177.9pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Anomaly scan &amp; EFW &gt; 10th centile.</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:97pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Serial USG from 28 weeks in women with congenital uterine anomalies till delivery.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">* Serial USG from 32 weeks in women with large fibroids and high BMI.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
