<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18134]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Anti D recommendations:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18135]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Anti D as soon as possible to women with negative blood group.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18136]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Keilhauer</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> test in all women to detect amount of FMH.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18137]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>In large FMH, anti D dose according to </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Keilhauer</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> test and repeat test after 48 hours to ensure fetal red cells have cleared.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18138]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Anti D should be given within 72 hours’ maximum up to 10 days.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18139]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Baby blood group is determined by fetal DNA.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18140]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Persistent kleihau</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>e</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>r positive can be due to Large FMH or Negative blood group of </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>babies</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18141]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Sex determination of Baby:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18142]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Examination by Senior persons that can be.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18143]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Expert midwife.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18144]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Obstetrician.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18145]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Neonatologist.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18146]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Pathologist.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18147]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Genetic sex determination.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18148]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>On placental tissue, skin.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18149]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>QF, PCR – determines y chromosomes markers, that is highly accurate and available within 2 days.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18150]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Fish – rapid sex determination.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18151]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Cell culture – longer time.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18152]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Post mortem – longer time.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18153]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Indeterminate sex – can be registered if still not determined.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18154]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Post mortem Examination:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18155]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Offered to all women with IUD.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18156]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Helpful in determining the cause of IUD.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18157]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><em><strong>Discussion with women</strong></em></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18158]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>In quiet, peaceful place.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18159]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Adequate time at least dedicated 1 hour.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18160]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Give detailed information regarding types of examination, what will happen in each type, Advantages, disadvantages of each type.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18161]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Place of examination.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18162]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>How tissues will be discarded.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18163]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Dignity care of baby.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18164]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Women </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>have</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> right to refuse the given consent. </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18165]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Types of post mortem:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18166]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Standard:</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18167]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Complete:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18168]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Carried out by pathologist.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18169]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Detailed examination, opening of body</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>cavities </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18170]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>taking samples.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18171]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>External examination by g</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>eneticist</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18172]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Limited:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18173]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>External examination by geneticist.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18174]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Carried out by pathologist.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18175]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Limited examination, mainly taking biopsies.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18176]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Laparoscopically can be carried out.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18177]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Image directed biopsies can be taken.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18178]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18179]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Alternative:</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18180]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Offered to those who decline std post mortem.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18181]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>USG:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18182]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Highest sensitivity to brain.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18183]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Lowest sensitivity to cardiothoracic anomalies.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18184]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>MRI:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18185]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Offered if interval between death and birth is &gt; 24 hours or </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>cardiothoracic anomalies are suspected.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18186]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>X – ray:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18187]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>When suspected skeletal anomaly.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18188]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Physical, psychological &amp; Social Care:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18189]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Offer individualized cultural approach.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18190]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Offer support groups – SANDS.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18191]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Involve other family for counselling like grandparents &amp; children because they are at    ed risk of PTSD.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18192]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Discuss with parents regarding:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18193]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Spending time.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18194]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Washing and dressing.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18195]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Taking photos, palm prints.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18196]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Making memories.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18197]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Describing babies features if they refuse to see baby.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18198]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Holding baby help in coping with grief and beneficial in their future well-being.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18199]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Legal requirement for </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>medical</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong> certification:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18200]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Still birth must be medically certified by fully registered doctor or midwife, who was present at birth or examined the baby after birth.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18201]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>HM coroner must be contacted if there is doubt about status of birth. Babies born later than 24 weeks who are known to have died before 24 weeks, do not have to be registered.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18202]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>The baby can be registered as indeterminate sex awaiting further tests.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18203]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Parents are responsible in law for registration of baby’s birth but can delegate task to health care professional.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18204]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Burial, Spiritual Guidance &amp; Remembrance:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18205]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Burial should be by parents but can delegate to hospital services after filling the form.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18206]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Parents should be provided proper guidance regarding C</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>remation</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18207]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Follow – Up:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18208]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Call when all results are available, if results are delayed then arrange an interim visit.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18209]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Before discharge inform all review processes.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18210]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Follow up discussion includes:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18211]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Cause of IUD, chance of recurrence, means of prevention of IUD.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18212]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Pre – pregnancy advice including support for smoking cessation.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18213]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Weight management.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18214]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Next pregnancy/ conception timing.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18215]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Care of subsequent Pregnancy:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18216]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Consultant led care.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18217]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Pregnancy following IUD due to placental cause.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18218]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Aspirin 150mg.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18219]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Umbilical artery Doppler every 3 – 4 weeks after 26 – 28 weeks.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18220]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Pregnancy following IUD due to </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>macrosomia</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>, vascular malformations, delayed maturity.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18221]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>GDM screening in subsequent pregnancy.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18222]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Pregnancy following IUD due to unexplained cause.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18223]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Aspirin 150mg.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18224]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>LMWH not routinely recommended except because of thromboembolic reason.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18225]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Continuous support during pregnancy.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18226]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>I</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>0L @ 39 weeks.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18227]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>C – section is an informed choice, not recommended routinely.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[18228]"> </p>', 1);

