<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19176]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Vaccines given in special circumstances:</strong></u></span></p>
<div class="mm-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0"><table class="mm-table" style="border-collapse:collapse;margin-left:0pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;"><colgroup><col style="width:84.45pt;"><col style="width:167.05pt;"></colgroup><tbody><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;">Vaccines</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;margin-bottom:8pt;">Indications</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Hep A</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:18pt;margin-bottom:8pt;">1.  Long term liver disease.</p><ol style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 36pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">1.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Hemophilia.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">2.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Poor sanitary condition.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">3.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Living near to sewage.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">4.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Living with primates.</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+0025 U+0031 U+002E"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">5.</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Drug abusers.</li></ol></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Hep B</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">1. Sex workers.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">2. Living with Hep B positive.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">3. Drug abusers.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">4. Multiple sex partners.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">5. Regular transfusions.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">6. Liver disease or CKD.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">7. Travelling to endemic areas.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Meningococcal </p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">1. Asplenia.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">2. Immune suppression.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">3. Complement deficiency.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">4. High risk endemics travel.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">5. University students &lt; 25 years of age</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">6. Contact with infected individuals.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Pneumococcal</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">1. Asplenia.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">2. SCD.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">3. Splenectomy.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">4. HIV.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Typhoid </p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">1. Travel to endemics.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Rabies</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">- Post exposure prophylaxis recommended</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">- Pre – exposure prophylaxis – where risk of exposure to rabies is substantial.</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:55.2pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Yellow fever</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:199.7pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">- High case fatality.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">- Given when travel is un avoidable.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
