<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19223]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Use of contrast enhance accuracy</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19224]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Commonly used contrast in CT </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>is</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> iodine containing =&gt; Maternal effects.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19225]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Also,</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> cross placenta but no fetal effects in animal’s studies.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19226]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19227]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Types of Examination: </strong></u></span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Fetal Radiation dose:</strong></u></span></p>
