solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Low – moderate dose – 0.01 – 10mGy</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Abdominal x – ray </p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Lumber spine</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">CT chest or pulmonary angiography</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Technetium as bone scintigraphy</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Pulmonary digital subtraction angiogram</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">CT – pelvimetry</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"> </p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">0.1 – 3.0</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">1 – 10 </p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">0.1 – 0.5</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">4 – 5 </p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">0.5</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">&lt; 1</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Higher doses – 10 – 50mGy</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Abdominal – CT</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Pelvic CT.</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;text-indent:-18pt;">F – FDG PET/ CT whole body</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">1.3 – 35.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">10 – 50.</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">10 – 50.</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19228]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19229]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19230]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19231]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19232]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19233]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19234]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19235]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>USG:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19236]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Thermal effect.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19237]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Mechanical effect.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19238]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Tissue damage by these (2) effects,   in Doppler,     in B – mode.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19239]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Cavitation:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19240]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Inertial – transient.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19241]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Non inertial – stable.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19242]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>More effect if exposure exceeds 60 min.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19243]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>MRI:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19244]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Challenging in </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>obstetrics</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> – to perform and interpret due to fetal movements, MRI better than USG, Safe at any Gestation.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19245]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u>Gadolinium contrast:</u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19246]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Improve imaging – crosses placenta and fetal circulation and excreted in amniotic fluid =&gt; risk of fibrosis in nephrogenic system (not) statistically significant.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19247]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Risk of SB and neonatal death.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19248]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Risk of rheumatological, inflammatory skin diseases.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19249]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Avoid –</strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> Gadolinium in pregnancy.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19250]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Nuclear imaging:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19251]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Thyroid scan, bone scan, Renal scan, V/P scan.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19252]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Most commonly use “isotope – tech 99)</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19253]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Gamma </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>rays emitted t/2 = 6 hours.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19254]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>“rad iodine 13” t/2 = 8 days.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19255]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Cause fetal hypothyroidism in 10 – 12 weeks.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19256]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>“F – FDG” in PET CT.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19257]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Avoid –</strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> Rad Iodine in pregnancy</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19258]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> Tech 99 &amp; F – FDG can be used =&gt; in thyroid scan use Tech 99 in place of radio Iodine.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19259]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>V/P Scan/ CTPA:</strong></u></span></p>
