<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19457]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Recommendations of Steroids:</strong></u></span></p>
<div class="mm-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0"><table class="mm-table" style="border-collapse:collapse;margin-left:0pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;"><colgroup><col style="width:269.75pt;"><col style="width:269.75pt;"></colgroup><tbody><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Before 24 weeks</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Discuss</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">24 – 34+6 weeks where preterm is anticipated</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Discuss and offer</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">35 – 36+6</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Consider the balance of risks and benefits</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Twins and triplets</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Targeted steroid same as singleton</p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Only targeted used</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Diabetes Mellitus</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 18pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Not a contraindication</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Additional insulin and close monitoring</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Steroid discussion with women or her carer @ 37 – 38+6 weeks about the risk and benefits, corticosteroids are associated with neonatal hypoglycemia.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Hypertension</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 18pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Offer after discussion in case of planned early birth</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Offer to SGA, FGR babies if birth is expected earlier but inform regarding lack of evidence.</li></ul></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">PPROM</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:269.75pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><ul style="list-style-type:none;margin:0 0 0 18pt;padding:0;text-indent:-18pt;"><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Offer if birth is expected to be preterm</li><li data-source-marker-codepoints="U+F0B7" data-source-marker-font="Symbol"><span class="list-prefix" style="display:inline-flex;width:18pt;"><span class="list-marker">•</span><span class="list-tab" aria-hidden="true" data-list-suffix="tab" style="flex:1 1 auto;min-width:0;"></span></span>Limited evidence to recommend repeat courses, however further courses may reduce need for neonatal respiratory support.</li></ul></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19458]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19459]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19460]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19461]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19462]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Dose and route of Steroids:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19463]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u>Dexamethasone Phosphate</u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>, I/M:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19464]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>24 mg</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19465]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19466]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>2 doses</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>4 doses</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19467]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>12 mg</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>6 mg</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19468]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>24 hours apart</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-tab" aria-hidden="true">	</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>12 hours apart</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19469]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>Betamethasone sodium Phosphate/ Acetate mix, I/M:</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19470]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>24mg total</span></p>', 0);
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-book-t-mm-09-033-1', 't-mm-09-033', 'document_html', '<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19471]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>2 doses</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19472]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 11pt''>24 hours apart</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19473]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>How long after Administration is a course more effective:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19474]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>After 48 hours of dose, Neonatal death is reduced.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19475]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>After 24 hours of 1</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>st</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> dose, benefits seen</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19476]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Most effective in reducing RDS if birth occurs between 24 hours to 7 days of 2</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>nd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> dose.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19477]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Contraindications of Steroid:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19478]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Systemic infections</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19479]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>In case of serious concerns, birth should not be delayed to administer steroid</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19480]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Repeat Course of Steroids:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19481]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>No reduction in serious morbidity or </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>long-term</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> benefits to babies instead risk of low birth weight and reduced length</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19482]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Limited evidence to recommend repeat course of steroid.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19483]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Repeat course reduce need for neonatal respiratory support</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19484]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Repeat courses </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>should not exceed three. </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19485]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19486]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19487]"> </p>', 1);

DELETE FROM content_blocks WHERE topic_id = 't-mm-09-034';
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-book-t-mm-09-034-0', 't-mm-09-034', 'document_html', '<div class="mm-release-marker" data-mm-release="f94027611ab71565c9dfd689046bb4a24db921b97ef1453416d5acfa140ed605" data-mm-topic="t-mm-09-034" hidden></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19488]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 16pt''><strong>21. </strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 16pt''><strong>CERVICAL CERCLAGE</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19489]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Definitions</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19490]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><em><strong>History indicated Cerclage:</strong></em></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19491]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Cerclage as a result of factors in a women’s obstetric or gyaecological history which     the risk of spontaneous 2</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>nd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> loss or preterm birth.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19492]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Prophylactic cerclage</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19493]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Offer @ 11 – 14 weeks.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19494]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><em><strong>Ultrasound indicated cerclage:</strong></em></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19495]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Cerclage is inserted as a therapeutic measure in cases of cervical length shortening seen on transvaginal ultrasound.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19496]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Prophylactic length is measured between 14 – 24 weeks by TVS and with an empty bladder</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19497]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Done if cervical length is &lt;25m @ gestation &lt;24 weeks.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19498]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><em><strong>Emergency cerclage/ Physical exam indicated cerclage:</strong></em></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19499]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Insertion of cerclage as salvage measure in case of premature cervical dilatation with exposed fetal membranes in vagina</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19500]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Pt </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>can present with vaginal dischar</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ge, bleeding or sensation of pressure</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19501]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Can be applied </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>up to</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> 27</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>+6</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> weeks </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19502]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Types of Cerclage:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19503]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Transvaginal (McDonald):</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19504]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Suture placed @ cervical isthmus junction without bladder mobilization.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19505]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>High transvaginal cerclage (</strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Shirodkar</strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>)</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19506]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Purse stri</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ng suture placed following bladder mobilization, to allow insertion above the level of cardinal ligaments.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19507]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Transabdominal Cerclage:</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19508]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Suture performed via laparotomy or laparoscopy, placing the suture @ </strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>cervico</strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong> </strong></em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>isthmic junction.</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19509]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Occlusion Cerclage:</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19510]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Occlusion of external OS by placement of a continuous non-absorbable suture. </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19511]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Purpose is the retention of mucus plug. </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19512]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Recommendations of Cervical Cerclage:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19513]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>History indicated</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19514]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> 3 or more preterm birth or 2</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>nd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> miscarriages.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19515]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>It reduces perinatal death</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19516]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>No benefit of this cerclage to those who has previous cervical surgery or uterine anomalies</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19517]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>It is unknown that the characteristics of previous events are helpful or not (painless dilatation, rupture of membranes, prior cervical surgery). </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19518]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Ultrasound indicated:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19519]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Not affected to those who has incidental short length in late 2</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>nd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> without risk factors.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19520]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Offered to those who had one or more preterm birth or 2</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>nd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>loss along with cervical length &lt;25mm measured @ &lt;24weeks.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19521]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Not offered to those who has cervical funneling without short cervical length &lt;25mm</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19522]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>USG surveillance of cervical length is offered to those who have previous preterm birth or 2</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>nd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> loss, by TVS with empty bladder and @ 16 – 24weeks, every 2 – 4weeks.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19523]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Other women where cervical length need to be measured are either high risk or intermediate risk.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19524]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>High Risk:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19525]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Previous PPROM &lt; 34 weeks</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19526]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Previous use of cerclage </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19527]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Known uterine variant </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19528]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Intrauterine adhesions</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19529]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>History of trachelectomy</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19530]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Intermediate Risk:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19531]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Previous</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> C/</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>S at</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>full dilatation </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19532]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>LLETZ with excision depth &gt;1cm, more </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19533]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>than 1 procedure or more than 1 cone biopsy.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19534]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Multiple Pregnancy:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19535]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>not offered either cerclage </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19536]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19537]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Raised BMI:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19538]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>BMI &gt;25, cerclage is effective in those who has cervical length &lt;25mm</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19539]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Transabdominal Cervical Cerclage:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19540]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Consider and discuss in women with f</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>a</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>iled or unsuccessful transvaginal cerclage</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19541]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Can be performed pre conceptually or in early pregnancy. Pre conceptually performed cerclage is more effective than antenatal cerclage. It is not associated with subfertility</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19542]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Can be performed laparoscopically</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19543]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Laparoscopy should be considered where possible as it has fewer complication.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19544]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>In case of delayed miscarriage or fetal death, decision of TOP is difficult </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>up to</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> 18 weeks suction curettage or dilatation and curettage can be performed via </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>stitch</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19545]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>&gt;18 weeks, </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>stitch</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> can be opened via posterior colpotomy. Failed colpotomy can led to hysterotomy or C/S. decision should be aided by senior obstetrician.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19546]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19547]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19548]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Emergency Cerclage:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19549]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Individualized decision by taking into account the risks and benefits.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19550]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Women’s decision should be aided by senior obstetrician </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19551]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>It can prolong pregnancy </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>up to</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> 34 weeks </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19552]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>It can reduce chance of birth by 2-fold before 34 weeks.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19553]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Advanced dilatation of cervix &gt; 4cm or membrane prolapse beyond external </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>o</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>s appears to be associated with higher cerclage failure.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19554]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Not justified beyond 24 weeks due to </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19555]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>potential risk of </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>iatrogenic</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> membrane rupture and subsequent preterm.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19556]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Contraindications of cerclage:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19557]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>1. </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>active preterm labour</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19558]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>2. </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>clinical </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Chorioamnionitis</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19559]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>3. </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>continuing vaginal bleeding.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19560]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>4. PPROM</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19561]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>5. Evidence of fetal defects</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19562]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>6. Lethal fetal defects</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19563]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>7. Fetal death</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19564]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Risk of cervical cerclage:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19565]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Small risk of intraoperative bladder damage, cervical trauma, membrane rupture, bleeding.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19566]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Cervical trauma/ laceration in case of labour with suture in place.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19567]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>High vaginal cerclage </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>needs</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> anaesthesia for insertion and removal.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19568]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>No association with PPROM, Chorioamnionitis IOL or C/S (except Emergency cerclage).</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19569]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>No association with preterm birth or 2</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>nd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> loss (except emergency cerclage).</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19570]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Risks and benefits should be discussed with women, both verbal and written information should be given before insertion of cerclage.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19571]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Investigation before cerclage insertion:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19572]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>1. History indicated cerclage.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19573]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>1</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>st</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> USG</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19574]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Aneuploidy screening</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19575]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>2. USG indicated or emergency cerclage anomaly scan.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19576]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>3. CRP + TLC count if clinical picture </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>exists</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19577]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>TLC cut off &lt;14,000/micro</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> liter</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19578]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>CRP cut off &lt;4 mg/dl</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19579]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>4. Amniocentesis</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19580]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>- No</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>t</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> before ultrasound or history indicated cerclage</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19581]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>- Can be done before emergency cerclage in cases where there is clinical suspicion of</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Intra amniotic infection.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19582]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>5. </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Amnioreduction</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19583]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>- No dat</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>a exists</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19584]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>6. Genital Screening </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19585]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>- Not undertaken routinely</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19586]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Operative issues:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19587]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Can be performed safely as day case procedure</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19588]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><em><strong>Tocolysis:</strong></em></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19589]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Consider on individual basis</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19590]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Not routinely</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19591]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><em><strong>Antibiotics before cerclage</strong></em></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19592]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Surgeon’s choice</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19593]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><em><strong>Anaesthesia</strong></em></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19594]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Decision by operating team along with women</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19595]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><em><strong>Suture material</strong></em></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19596]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Non absorbable suture, surgeon’s di</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>scretion.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19597]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><em><strong>Type of cerclage:</strong></em></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19598]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Depends on surgeon’s choice</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19599]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>High/ low cerclage has similar outcome.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19600]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Try to place suture in cervix as high as possible</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19601]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>No difference between two possible string or single suture. It’s surgeon’s discretion.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19602]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Occlusion suture in addition to primary suture not applied routinely</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19603]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Bed Rest:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19604]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Not recommended routinely</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19605]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Sexual intercourse:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19606]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Abstinence not recommended routinely.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19607]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Post cerclage serial USG for cervical length:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19608]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Not done routinely</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19609]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Selected USG indicated cerclage cases to offer timely steroid and in utero transfer.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19610]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Fetal </strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>fibronectin</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19611]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Not recommended routinely</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19612]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>High negative predictive value can reassure the women.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19613]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Progesterone supplementation:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19614]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Not recommended routinely</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19615]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Arabian pessary or progesterone</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19616]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>None of them is more effective than cerclage</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19617]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19618]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Removal of Cerclage:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19619]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>1. @ 36</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>+1</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> – 37weeks before labour</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19620]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>2. Women presenting in active labour, remove cerclage to prevent cervical trauma.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19621]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>3. Abdominal cerclage need not to be removed. Deliver by C/S and leave cerclage in place.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19622]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>PPROM and Cerclage removal:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19623]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>PPROM between 24 – 34 weeks + No infections =&gt; Delayed removal by 48 hours.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19624]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Delayed removal until labour ensures or birth indicated is associated with an     risk of maternal/fetal sepsis and is not recommended.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19625]"> </p>
