<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19837]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Individualized assessment in Birth Planning</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19838]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>History n</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>o</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>t</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>itself</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> a reason for advising birth in an </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>obs</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>tetric </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>unit</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> but indicate that further consideration of birth setting may be needed</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19839]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em>Table </em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em>45</em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em>. Medical conditions indicating individual assessment is needed when planning place of birth</em></span></p>
<div class="mm-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0"><table class="mm-table" style="border-collapse:collapse;table-layout:fixed;margin-left:5.3pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;"><colgroup><col style="width:97.25pt;"><col style="width:409.75pt;"></colgroup><tbody><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="358" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:97.25pt;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;padding-left:0.35pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Disease area</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:409.75pt;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;text-align:center;padding-left:0.35pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Medical condition</p></td></tr><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="510" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:97.25pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:4.1pt;margin-top:5.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Cardiovascular</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:409.75pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:40.1pt;margin-top:5.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Cardiac disease without intrapartum implications</p></td></tr><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="510" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:97.25pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:4.1pt;margin-top:5.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Disease area</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:409.75pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:40.1pt;margin-top:5.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Medical condition</p></td></tr><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="510" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:97.25pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:4.1pt;margin-top:5.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-top:5.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Haematological</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:409.75pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:40.45pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Atypical antibodies not putting the baby at risk of haemolytic disease</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:40.45pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Sickle-cell trait</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Thalassemia trait</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Anaemia – hemoglobin 85 to 105 g/liters at onset of labour</p></td></tr><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="510" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:97.25pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:4.1pt;margin-top:5.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Endocrine</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:409.75pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:40.1pt;margin-top:5.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Unstable hypothyroidism such that a change in treatment is needed</p></td></tr><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="510" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:97.25pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-top:5.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:4.1pt;margin-top:5.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:4.1pt;margin-top:5.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Infective</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:409.75pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:15.55pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Group B streptococcus where intrapartum intravenous antibiotics are recommended</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:15.55pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Hepatitis B or C with normal liver function tests (as baby will need paediatric review after birth)</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:15.55pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Carrier of or infected with HIV</p></td></tr><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="510" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:97.25pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:4.1pt;margin-top:5.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Immune</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:409.75pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:40.1pt;margin-top:5.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Non-specific connective tissue disorders</p></td></tr><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="510" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:97.25pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-top:5.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Skeletal/ Neurological</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:409.75pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Spinal abnormalities</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-top:0.05pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Previous fractured pelvis</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Neurological deficits</p></td></tr><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="510" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:97.25pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-top:5.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Gastrointestinal</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:409.75pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Liver disease without current abnormal liver function</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-top:0.05pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Crohn''s disease</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Ulcerative colitis</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19840]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19841]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 9pt''><em>Table </em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 9pt''><em>46</em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 9pt''><em>. </em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 9pt''><em>Other factors to take into account when planning place of birth</em></span></p>', 0);
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-book-t-mm-10-002-1', 't-mm-10-002', 'document_html', '<div class="mm-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0"><table class="mm-table" style="border-collapse:collapse;margin-left:0pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;"><colgroup><col style="width:84.8pt;"><col style="width:425.25pt;"></colgroup><tbody><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:84.8pt;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Factor</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:425.25pt;background-color:#B4C6E7;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Additional information</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:84.8pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Previous complications</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:425.25pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Stillbirth or neonatal death with a known non-recurrent cause</p><p style="margin:0;margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;margin-top:0.05pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Pre-eclampsia developing at term</p><p style="margin:0;margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Placental abruption with good outcome</p><p style="margin:0;margin-top:1.05pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">History of previous baby more than 4.5 kg</p><p style="margin:0;margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;padding-right:33.6pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Extensive vaginal, cervical, or third- or fourth-degree perineal trauma</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;margin-top:12.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Retained placenta needing manual removal in theatre</p><p style="margin:0;margin-top:1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;margin-top:0.05pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Previous term baby with jaundice requiring exchange transfusion</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;margin-top:0.05pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Major gynaecological surgery</p></td></tr><tr><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:84.8pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:8pt;">Current pregnancy</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:425.25pt;border-top:0.5pt solid #000000;border-right:0.5pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.5pt solid #000000;border-left:0.5pt solid #000000;padding-top:0pt;padding-right:5.4pt;padding-bottom:0pt;padding-left:5.4pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:39.4pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Antepartum bleeding of unknown origin (single episode after 24 weeks of pregnancy)</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:20.9pt;margin-top:12.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Body mass index (BMI) at booking (see the section on impact of BMI on choice of place of birth)</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:0.4pt;margin-top:12.05pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Blood pressure of 140 mmHg systolic or 90 mmHg diastolic or more on 2 occasions</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;padding-right:0.4pt;margin-top:12.05pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Clinical or ultrasound suspicion of macrosomia</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Induction of labour</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Grand multiparity (parity 4 or more)</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-top:0.05pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Recreational drug use</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Under current outpatient psychiatric care</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Age 40 or over at booking</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Fibroids</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Fetal abnormality</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19842]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19843]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19844]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Care during labor:</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19845]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>One to one in all setting.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19846]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Communication:</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19847]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Clear, comprehensive, welcoming.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19848]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Empower women in decision making.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19849]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Explain all procedures and observations before they take place.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19850]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Take consen</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>t before examination or any interventio</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>n</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19851]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19852]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Respect personal space, privacy and dignity</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19853]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Calm, confident, professional approach.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19854]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Make sure women is knowing about pain relief options.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19855]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Position and mobilization:</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19856]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Adapt whatever position she finds comfortable except lying flat on back.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19857]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Encourage mobilization.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19858]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Upright position = </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19859]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Reduce pain</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19860]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Short</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>en</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> 1</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>st</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> stage up to1 hour and 20 min.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19861]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Short</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>en</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> 2</span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>nd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> stage </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19862]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Less c – section, instrumental birth.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19863]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Blood loss.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19864]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Support:</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19865]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Encourage women to have support from birth companion of her choice.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19866]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em><strong>Hygiene measures</strong></em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19867]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Tap water for cleaning before examination.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19868]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Routine hygiene measures by staff</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[19869]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>PPE according to risks of exposure.</span></p>', 1);

