<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20328]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>1.</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Oxytocin I/M, 10 units.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20329]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>2</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>. </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Oxytocin I/V, 5 units over 2 – 3</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>min, If</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> women have received oxytocin in 1</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>st</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> o</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>r </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>2</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>nd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> stage</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20330]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>3</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Oxytocin plus ergometrine I/M 5 units </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>  </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>+ 500mg</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20331]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>More effective than oxytocin alone</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20332]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Advised if there are risk factors of PPH</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20333]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>More nausea and vomiting as compared to oxytocin alone.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20334]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u>C/I:</u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20335]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>1) </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Severe hypertension</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20336]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>2) </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Pre – Eclampsia</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20337]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>3) </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Eclampsia</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20338]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>4) </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Severe cardiac problem</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20339]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>5) </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Hepatic disease</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20340]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>6) </span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##2F5496; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Renal disease</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20341]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Offer antiemetic to women having both oxytocin and ergometrine</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20342]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>4</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Carbetocin, slow I/V, in women who has C/S.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20343]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>5</strong></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>.</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Don’t use cord oxytocin or prostaglandins.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20344]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''><u><em><strong>Cord clamping and cutting</strong></em></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20345]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Clamp the cord before 5 min in order to perform CCT.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20346]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Don’t clamp before 1 min unless</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20347]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>B</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>aby’s heart beat &lt; 60 and not getting better.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20348]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Concern’s regarding integrity of cord.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20349]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Women’s choice.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20350]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em>Co</em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em>n</em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em>vert passive management to active management in case of:</em></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20351]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>PPH</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20352]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Placenta not delivered after 1 hours.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20353]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Prolonged 3</strong></u></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup><u><strong>rd</strong></u></sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong> stage:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20354]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Failed delivery of placenta after birth of baby.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20355]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Active &gt; 30 min</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20356]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Passive &gt; 1 hour</span></p>', 0);

DELETE FROM content_blocks WHERE topic_id = 't-mm-10-007';
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-book-t-mm-10-007-0', 't-mm-10-007', 'document_html', '<div class="mm-release-marker" data-mm-release="f94027611ab71565c9dfd689046bb4a24db921b97ef1453416d5acfa140ed605" data-mm-topic="t-mm-10-007" hidden></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20357]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''>RETAINED PLACENTA</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20358]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Save I/V line</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20359]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Don’t give umbilical cord oxytocin</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20360]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Don’t give I/V oxytocin routinely unless women </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>are</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> bleeding excessively</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20361]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Offer vaginal examination to assess the need for manual removal, explain that it is painful and also offer analgesia.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20362]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Transfer to obs unit if not already in</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20363]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Give good analgesia – no manual removal without an anesthetist.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20364]"> </p>', 0);

DELETE FROM content_blocks WHERE topic_id = 't-mm-10-008';
INSERT INTO content_blocks (id, topic_id, type, content, `order`) VALUES ('cb-book-t-mm-10-008-0', 't-mm-10-008', 'document_html', '<div class="mm-release-marker" data-mm-release="f94027611ab71565c9dfd689046bb4a24db921b97ef1453416d5acfa140ed605" data-mm-topic="t-mm-10-008" hidden></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20365]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##FFFFFF; font-family: "Calibri Light", sans-serif; font-size: 14pt''>POSTPARTUM HEMORRHAGE</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20366]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Risk factors for PPH</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20367]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Antenatal:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20368]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Previous PPH requiring blood transfusion</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20369]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Placenta accreta spectrum</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20370]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Pre – Eclampsia</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20371]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Hb &lt; 85 g/lit @ time of labor</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20372]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>BMI &gt; 35</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20373]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Grand multi &gt; 4 or more</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20374]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>APH or abruption</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20375]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Existing uterine abnormalities like fibroids.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20376]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Low lying placenta</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20377]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Use of SSRI or SNRI one month before delivery.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20378]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><u><strong>Intrapartum:</strong></u></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20379]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>IOL or Augmentation with oxytocin or prostaglandin</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20380]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Prolonged 1</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>st</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> or 2</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><sup>nd</sup></span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> stage.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20381]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Sepsis </span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20382]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Oxytocin </span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>uses</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''> during labor</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20383]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Precipitated labor</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20384]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Instrumental birth</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20385]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Shoulder dystocia</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20386]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Delay in delivery of placenta.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20387]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20388]"><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em>Table </em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em>47</em></span><span class="mm-run" style=''color: ##44546A; font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><em>. Choice of uterotonics for the treatment of postpartum haemorrhage because of uterine atony</em></span></p>
<div class="mm-table-scroll" role="region" tabindex="0"><table class="mm-table" style="border-collapse:collapse;table-layout:fixed;margin-left:5.3pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;"><colgroup><col style="width:82.35pt;"><col style="width:147.5pt;"><col style="width:90.5pt;"><col style="width:186.7pt;"></colgroup><tbody><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="1080" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:82.35pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:0.35pt;margin-top:5.05pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Uterotonic used in the third stage of labour as prophylaxis</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:147.5pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:0.35pt;padding-right:1.45pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Suggested first-line treatment of postpartum haemorrhage</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:90.5pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:0.35pt;padding-right:25.6pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Suggested second-line treatment of postpartum haemorrhage</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:186.7pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:0.35pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Additional treatments that can be offered, depending on clinical need</p></td></tr><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="1080" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:82.35pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:0.35pt;margin-top:5.05pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:0.35pt;margin-top:5.05pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:0.35pt;margin-top:5.05pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">No uterotonic used – physiological management</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:147.5pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;padding-right:3.75pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Oxytocin plus ergometrine by intramuscular injection (if contraindicated, give carboprost), or</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Oxytocin infusion as soon as intravenous access is available</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:90.5pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:0.35pt;padding-right:25.6pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:0.35pt;padding-right:25.6pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:0.35pt;padding-right:25.6pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:0.35pt;padding-right:25.6pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:0.35pt;padding-right:25.6pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:0.35pt;padding-right:25.6pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Carboprost intramuscular injection</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:186.7pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;padding-right:4.9pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Carboprost intramuscular injection (can be repeated at intervals not less than</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;margin-top:0.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">15 minutes up to a maximum of 8 doses), or</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:36pt;margin-top:0.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-18pt;">Misoprostol 800 micrograms sublingually or rectally (may be used earlier if intravenous route not available)</p><p style="margin:0;margin-top:5pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p></td></tr><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="3988" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:82.35pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-top:10.65pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:4.1pt;padding-right:26.8pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Oxytocin alone</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:147.5pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-top:9.3pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;padding-right:7.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Ergometrine intramuscular injection (if contraindicated give carboprost), or</p><p style="margin:0;text-align:justify;padding-left:23.7pt;padding-right:8.4pt;margin-top:12.2pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Oxytocin infusion as soon as intravenous access is available</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:90.5pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-top:1.65pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:4.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Carboprost intramuscular injection</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:186.7pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-top:0.3pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;padding-right:4.9pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Carboprost intramuscular injection (can be repeated at intervals not less than</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;margin-top:0.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">15 minutes up to a maximum of 8 doses), or</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;padding-right:3.25pt;margin-top:12.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Misoprostol 800 micrograms sublingually or rectally (may be used earlier if intravenous route not available)</p></td></tr><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="3988" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:82.35pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-top:1.65pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:4.1pt;padding-right:6pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Oxytocin plus ergometrine</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:147.5pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-top:12.8pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;padding-right:46.05pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Carboprost intramuscular injection, or</p><p style="margin:0;text-align:justify;padding-left:23.7pt;padding-right:8.4pt;margin-top:12.15pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Oxytocin infusion as soon as intravenous access is available</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:90.5pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-top:7.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:4.1pt;margin-top:0.05pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Repeat carboprost after</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:4.1pt;margin-top:0.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">15 minutes</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:186.7pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-top:0.3pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;padding-right:4.9pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Carboprost intramuscular injection (can be repeated at intervals not less than</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;margin-top:0.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">15 minutes up to a maximum of 8 doses), or</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;padding-right:3.25pt;margin-top:12.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Misoprostol 800 micrograms sublingually or rectally (may be used earlier if intravenous route not available)</p></td></tr><tr data-mm-row-height-twips="3268" data-mm-row-height-rule="auto"><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:82.35pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-top:1.65pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:4.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Carbetocin</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:147.5pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-top:7.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:4.1pt;padding-right:1.45pt;margin-top:0.05pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Ergometrine intramuscular injection</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:90.5pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;margin-top:12.6pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:4.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">Carboprost intramuscular injection</p></td><td style="white-space:pre-wrap;width:186.7pt;border-top:0.75pt solid #000000;border-right:0.75pt solid #000000;border-bottom:0.75pt solid #000000;border-left:0.75pt solid #000000;padding-right:0pt;padding-left:0pt;"><p style="margin:0;margin-top:0.3pt;margin-bottom:0pt;"></p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;padding-right:4.9pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Carboprost intramuscular injection (can be repeated at intervals not less than</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;margin-top:0.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;">15 minutes up to a maximum of 8 doses), or</p><p style="margin:0;padding-left:23.7pt;padding-right:5.45pt;margin-top:12.1pt;margin-bottom:0pt;text-indent:-14.75pt;">Misoprostol 800 micrograms sublingually or rectally</p></td></tr></tbody></table></div>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20389]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20390]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20391]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20392]"> </p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20393]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Repeat dose of ergometrine or combination of oxytocin and ergometrine may be given if other medicines are not available like home birth</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20394]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Oxytocin onset of action 2 .5min</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20395]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Effect lasts for 30min.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20396]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Ergometrine onset of action 7 min</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20397]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Effect lasts for 3 hours.</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20398]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''><strong>Management Algorithm:</strong></span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20399]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>Follow GTG</span></p>
<p class="mm-para" data-mm-source-path="word/document.xml/w:document[1]/w:body[1]/w:p[20400]"><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>As desc</span><span class="mm-run" style=''font-family: "Calibri", sans-serif; font-size: 12pt''>ribed in post-partum hemorrhage, (Postpartum module)</span></p>', 0);

